WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:14.666
NETFLIX PRESENTS

2
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:24.708
What's this?

3
00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:30.958
<i>The person you have called
can't be reached at the moment. Please...</i>

4
00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:32.666
This fucking phone.

5
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:41.833
Fuck.

6
00:00:55.541 --> 00:00:56.416
Wow!

7
00:00:57.041 --> 00:00:58.000
Wow, wow, wow.

8
00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:59.791
So you hang out here?

9
00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:01.666
I don't remember. I'm allowed? Thanks.

10
00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:02.875
That's what I remember.

11
00:01:02.958 --> 00:01:04.125
How much did you drink?

12
00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.583
What are you saying, Beril?

13
00:01:07.416 --> 00:01:09.208
How are you? What are you doing?

14
00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:11.541
What I need to do. You?

15
00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:13.875
I'm waiting for Nazım.
I forgot my jacket here.

16
00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:14.958
Is he here?

17
00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.125
He never leaves. He's always here.

18
00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:18.916
Next time, I'll give it to the poor.

19
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.291
- Seksek!
- Nazım.

20
00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:22.166
- How are you?
- Good, you?

21
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.958
- Good. Welcome.
- Thanks.

22
00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:26.000
- Want a drink? You sure?
- No, babe. Thanks.

23
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.958
- I'm off. Thanks.
- You should stay.

24
00:01:28.041 --> 00:01:30.416
You know what? You can stay if you want.

25
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.833
- Really?
- Yeah.

26
00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:34.916
Dude, we're always here.
The question is if you can stay.

27
00:01:35.458 --> 00:01:37.375
- Where are you, Semih?
- Right here.

28
00:01:38.041 --> 00:01:40.166
I think you are a bit late. Just a bit.

29
00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:43.250
I have a café now. It's one street over.

30
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:45.208
- Be sure to stop by.
- Okay.

31
00:01:45.291 --> 00:01:46.541
If it won't be a problem.

32
00:01:47.125 --> 00:01:48.458
I don't like problems.

33
00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:49.708
I don't want problems.

34
00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:52.041
- I'm off. Kisses. Bye.
- Where are you going?

35
00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:53.500
Has it been three years?

36
00:01:56.083 --> 00:01:58.333
- What?
- We last met three years ago?

37
00:01:58.416 --> 00:01:59.750
I haven't kept track, dude.

38
00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:02.791
You named this place,
but never came to congratulate me for it.

39
00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.875
See, I'm right here. Let's toast.

40
00:02:07.458 --> 00:02:08.625
How is it?

41
00:02:10.083 --> 00:02:10.916
Awesome.

42
00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:13.541
I'll stick it everywhere.

43
00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:14.500
Where is Defne?

44
00:02:16.875 --> 00:02:17.916
No!

45
00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:19.958
He won't tell.

46
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:57.458
- What the hell?
- Oh, shit!

47
00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:00.666
I'm fucking soaked!

48
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.750
What was that?
Do you kiss every woman who smiles at you?

49
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:05.625
No, of course not!

50
00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:08.916
It's different
when they smile out of love.

51
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.500
More like out of kindness.

52
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:12.875
Maybe you should meet? Semih.

53
00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:15.791
- Why should we?
- He's right. We should. What's your name?

54
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:19.041
- Why do you need my name?
- To use it in a sentence. May I?

55
00:03:19.833 --> 00:03:22.166
- Are you always like this?
- Like what?

56
00:03:22.791 --> 00:03:24.416
A bit weird.

57
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.958
You know, weird is just
a side effect of being awesome.

58
00:03:27.041 --> 00:03:28.750
That quote has a different context.

59
00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:30.500
Context? Concept?

60
00:03:30.583 --> 00:03:32.458
- Your high school?
- German School of Istanbul.

61
00:03:32.541 --> 00:03:35.375
<i>Entschuldigung.</i>
We ran out of concepts for the day.

62
00:03:35.958 --> 00:03:37.250
- We have whiskey.
- Oh?

63
00:03:37.333 --> 00:03:39.208
- And wine.
- What else?

64
00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:41.000
What's your name?

65
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:42.791
What's the rush? What's up with you?

66
00:03:42.875 --> 00:03:45.791
- Look, I'm soaking wet!
- You deserved worse.

67
00:03:45.875 --> 00:03:47.208
- Please, Defne!
- What's up, Def?

68
00:03:47.291 --> 00:03:49.166
Semih is like a brother to me.

69
00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.041
And let me tell you,
he is normally a great guy, but...

70
00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:55.291
But he is a bit weird today.

71
00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:59.166
- Nazım, you idiot. Move!
- Wait. Where are you going? Hey!

72
00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.166
- Look.
- What?

73
00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.250
We'll all be at the studio this weekend.

74
00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.166
Defne will be there too.

75
00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:06.375
We have a nice studio.

76
00:04:12.083 --> 00:04:13.916
<i>There are footprints in front of me.</i>

77
00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:16.750
<i>Which means somebody was here.</i>

78
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:28.333
Wow, Semih! Look who's here.

79
00:04:28.416 --> 00:04:30.583
I'm just hanging around.

80
00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:33.916
I have a class now. It will take an hour.

81
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.041
- Let's make you a workout plan.
- Okay.

82
00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:38.000
- All right.
- Thanks.

83
00:04:39.458 --> 00:04:42.500
Ares, don't you have
a class with Defne today?

84
00:04:43.125 --> 00:04:44.500
She cancelled.

85
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:46.708
I see. Thanks. Cool.

86
00:05:21.666 --> 00:05:24.750
Semih, I hope I didn't disturb you
coming so late.

87
00:05:24.833 --> 00:05:25.666
No problem.

88
00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.041
I called Defne. We need to renew
our contract at the end of this month.

89
00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:34.000
She said you broke up and I should discuss
the rent increase with you.

90
00:05:34.708 --> 00:05:39.291
So I came to talk to you.
But it's not urgent. I can come later.

91
00:05:40.375 --> 00:05:41.500
She said we broke up?

92
00:06:28.541 --> 00:06:31.041
You actually came to work, huh?

93
00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:32.625
What's going on?

94
00:06:33.583 --> 00:06:34.666
She's super stressed.

95
00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.541
I bet some shit went down with Uğur.

96
00:06:36.625 --> 00:06:37.583
She's coming.

97
00:06:37.666 --> 00:06:40.000
You get it then. No need to talk further.

98
00:06:40.083 --> 00:06:42.625
How are you, honey?
Yezdan said you were sick.

99
00:06:42.708 --> 00:06:44.166
I'm good, thank you.

100
00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.125
- Great, I need you.
- Okay.

101
00:06:49.125 --> 00:06:52.291
Maybe you should ask
what she needs you for, huh?

102
00:06:52.375 --> 00:06:53.291
Shut up, Özge.

103
00:06:53.375 --> 00:06:57.166
You don't know how upset she was in there.
But she is so nice to you.

104
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:01.208
But she is right. The customers are crazy.
You can't tell what they want.

105
00:07:01.708 --> 00:07:03.791
It's better to be like you, but...

106
00:07:04.916 --> 00:07:06.291
It's my fault that I care.

107
00:07:10.291 --> 00:07:13.291
God, when will I get to do
what I want to do?

108
00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:16.000
I want to play the guitar, but I can't.

109
00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:18.541
We don't go to concerts anymore.

110
00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:20.791
Nothing is enjoyable.
I can't stand anything.

111
00:07:20.875 --> 00:07:23.666
I know I'm getting old.
Things are different now.

112
00:07:24.416 --> 00:07:26.833
I'll die soon. Hopefully.
Or my husband can die.

113
00:07:26.916 --> 00:07:29.708
Or we can have a baby or something.
This routine...

114
00:07:29.791 --> 00:07:32.750
- Give me, you're struggling to read it.
- This fucking phone.

115
00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:35.833
What kind of phone is this?

116
00:07:35.916 --> 00:07:37.541
- It's broken. Is it Defne?
- Yes.

117
00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.291
She'll pick up her stuff.

118
00:07:41.666 --> 00:07:42.875
You two broke up?

119
00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:44.625
- Give me that.
- Huh?

120
00:07:44.708 --> 00:07:47.958
- Picking up your stuff?
- I had to read it when you couldn't.

121
00:07:48.041 --> 00:07:50.541
I don't know what's happening up there,
but it's awful.

122
00:07:50.625 --> 00:07:54.791
Maybe something is in retrograde.
Everybody is feeling down and unmotivated.

123
00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.541
You aren't upset, right?

124
00:07:58.583 --> 00:07:59.416
Hello?

125
00:07:59.916 --> 00:08:02.250
<i>Hi, I'm Hande
from Sevcen Real Estate Services.</i>

126
00:08:02.958 --> 00:08:03.791
Sorry, who?

127
00:08:04.416 --> 00:08:09.250
<i>You called and left a voice mail
saying you need help finding a new place.</i>

128
00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:11.833
<i>I didn't want to disturb you
over the weekend, so I'm calling now.</i>

129
00:08:12.583 --> 00:08:14.333
I never called you, madam. That's...

130
00:08:14.833 --> 00:08:16.083
<i>Hello?</i>

131
00:08:17.541 --> 00:08:19.666
<i>Yeah, help me find a place.</i>

132
00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.083
<i>Let's figure it out,
and I'll cry afterward.</i>

133
00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.583
<i>I'm hanging up now.
Good night, don't let the bedbugs bite.</i>

134
00:08:28.291 --> 00:08:29.375
I have a client here.

135
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:32.958
- I cut the corner piece.
- Come back later, for God's sake!

136
00:08:33.041 --> 00:08:35.458
Yes, I guess I did call you.

137
00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.833
It seems I used Nazım's phone.
My phone screen is broken.

138
00:08:38.916 --> 00:08:41.333
Let me tell you,
alcohol and phones don't mix.

139
00:08:41.416 --> 00:08:44.125
I sometimes drink and tweet all night.

140
00:08:44.208 --> 00:08:46.500
And in the morning I say,
"God, who wrote this stuff?"

141
00:08:46.583 --> 00:08:49.250
By the way, you didn't need
to come all the way here

142
00:08:49.333 --> 00:08:51.666
to tell me
you weren't looking for a place.

143
00:08:52.375 --> 00:08:53.916
- Nevzat! Two teas!
- What?

144
00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:57.083
Why are you here
if you aren't looking for a place?

145
00:08:57.166 --> 00:09:01.541
I'm not forcing you. I only wanted to help
because you called me.

146
00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:03.958
{\an8}Look, it says,
"Sevcen Real Estate Services."

147
00:09:04.041 --> 00:09:05.291
{\an8}So it's all good.

148
00:09:06.375 --> 00:09:08.291
What now? Are we looking for a place?

149
00:09:11.125 --> 00:09:13.000
<i>I feel so sad for them.</i>

150
00:09:13.083 --> 00:09:14.208
Nobody buys from them.

151
00:09:22.583 --> 00:09:24.250
What did you do to the seller?

152
00:09:24.333 --> 00:09:26.375
- I bought it, dude.
- Awesome.

153
00:09:26.875 --> 00:09:28.708
- There you go.
- I got it.

154
00:09:28.791 --> 00:09:30.958
- Go on.
- Let's enjoy some cotton candy!

155
00:09:36.541 --> 00:09:38.541
Wow, seriously?

156
00:09:40.791 --> 00:09:41.791
Imagine!

157
00:09:49.416 --> 00:09:51.541
Congratulations.
I heard you got a new job.

158
00:09:51.625 --> 00:09:53.750
We'll see if it is worth congratulating.

159
00:09:54.791 --> 00:09:56.166
You don't want it?

160
00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:58.000
No, it's not that.

161
00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.583
My mom kind of forced me into it.

162
00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:01.833
- Oh.
- Yeah.

163
00:10:01.916 --> 00:10:04.208
So you had to take the job.

164
00:10:05.166 --> 00:10:07.291
Had to? It's not that I had to.

165
00:10:07.375 --> 00:10:08.375
What then?

166
00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:11.666
I just don't want to be
a burden on her anymore.

167
00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.041
What's your real job?

168
00:10:13.125 --> 00:10:14.208
You're really asking?

169
00:11:02.833 --> 00:11:06.458
Yes, these are my babies.

170
00:11:09.083 --> 00:11:10.083
Well done.

171
00:11:10.833 --> 00:11:13.166
But they don't pay the bills.

172
00:11:15.041 --> 00:11:17.666
- And things that pay the bills aren't fun.
- Wow.

173
00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.250
So appreciate your job.

174
00:11:20.666 --> 00:11:21.500
Okay.

175
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:22.916
Thanks.

176
00:11:27.041 --> 00:11:27.875
How about this?

177
00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:32.041
You can make money,
and I can do the fun stuff.

178
00:11:32.125 --> 00:11:33.166
What do you say?

179
00:11:34.166 --> 00:11:36.083
Being a burden on me will bother you.

180
00:11:36.666 --> 00:11:38.041
Hell no!

181
00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:46.291
<i>Did you really love her?</i>

182
00:11:47.541 --> 00:11:48.375
<i>She was different.</i>

183
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:49.916
<i>Different?</i>

184
00:11:50.416 --> 00:11:51.416
<i>Cool.</i>

185
00:11:54.416 --> 00:11:56.416
<i>But she wasn't that different.</i>

186
00:11:57.291 --> 00:11:59.291
<i>Were you the one who wanted to end it?</i>

187
00:12:00.125 --> 00:12:03.375
I mean, we were playing overtime.

188
00:12:03.458 --> 00:12:04.458
I guess.

189
00:12:04.958 --> 00:12:05.958
It happens.

190
00:12:06.041 --> 00:12:07.958
I can't stand playing overtime.

191
00:12:09.208 --> 00:12:11.083
You just end the game?

192
00:12:11.166 --> 00:12:12.333
I do.

193
00:12:12.416 --> 00:12:13.666
- I feel hot.
- Right away.

194
00:12:15.291 --> 00:12:16.291
All right.

195
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:18.291
- So...
- Huh?

196
00:12:18.875 --> 00:12:23.291
Do you have an ongoing game
I should know about?

197
00:12:23.375 --> 00:12:26.208
No. And I don't want one. I'm good.

198
00:12:27.708 --> 00:12:29.291
Try falling in love.

199
00:12:31.541 --> 00:12:32.666
It's great.

200
00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:35.250
I mean it.

201
00:12:37.541 --> 00:12:41.625
If I were to fall in love with every guy
who bought me cotton candy...

202
00:12:42.958 --> 00:12:43.791
{\an8}Oh!

203
00:12:43.875 --> 00:12:45.250
{\an8}A BIT WEIRD

204
00:12:45.333 --> 00:12:47.083
{\an8}Would it be a bit weird?

205
00:13:05.083 --> 00:13:05.958
What?

206
00:13:29.541 --> 00:13:30.708
Hey, Seksek!

207
00:13:32.375 --> 00:13:33.208
Semih!

208
00:13:36.541 --> 00:13:37.916
What's going on?

209
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.000
Nothing, dude.

210
00:13:44.750 --> 00:13:45.750
- Fuck!
- What happened?

211
00:13:46.666 --> 00:13:49.166
Dude, I slammed the door on my hand.

212
00:13:51.416 --> 00:13:53.291
I should have been the one to end it.

213
00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.625
We were playing overtime,
but I didn't notice.

214
00:13:56.708 --> 00:13:57.541
Fuck.

215
00:13:58.333 --> 00:14:00.125
Let's go to the ER if you are hurt.

216
00:14:00.208 --> 00:14:02.541
Don't worry,
I don't need two hands to shit on you.

217
00:14:03.958 --> 00:14:05.583
That's how we roll, boy!

218
00:14:05.666 --> 00:14:07.750
You lucked out.
You don't know about soccer.

219
00:14:07.833 --> 00:14:09.583
Don't be upset, bro.

220
00:14:10.291 --> 00:14:13.625
Maybe you'll be lucky in love,
but you score own goals there too.

221
00:14:19.041 --> 00:14:20.666
You see how she took everything?

222
00:14:23.166 --> 00:14:25.250
When did she even decide to do it?

223
00:14:27.166 --> 00:14:29.666
Looks like she had been considering it.

224
00:14:31.375 --> 00:14:32.500
Looks like it.

225
00:14:34.541 --> 00:14:35.375
Right?

226
00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:38.416
Of course, man.

227
00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:45.708
Otherwise, how could she do it so quickly,
as if in a mad rush?

228
00:14:48.791 --> 00:14:49.958
Have you talked to her?

229
00:14:51.333 --> 00:14:52.166
No.

230
00:14:53.583 --> 00:14:56.041
What? You never called each other?

231
00:14:56.916 --> 00:14:58.958
Why should I call her? It's over.

232
00:15:02.583 --> 00:15:04.208
I mean, what was the problem?

233
00:15:05.125 --> 00:15:08.000
I didn't cheat or anything.
I didn't do anything wrong.

234
00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.750
Seksek, my mom comes over twice a week.

235
00:15:11.833 --> 00:15:13.333
A cleaning lady, twice a week.

236
00:15:13.416 --> 00:15:14.958
A working girl, twice a week.

237
00:15:15.041 --> 00:15:16.458
And I get one day to myself.

238
00:15:17.458 --> 00:15:19.083
Anything more would be too much.

239
00:15:20.125 --> 00:15:21.416
It is too much for me.

240
00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.125
The same goes for you.

241
00:15:24.708 --> 00:15:25.666
It was sudden.

242
00:15:26.958 --> 00:15:28.958
I didn't expect it.
It was out of the blue.

243
00:15:29.041 --> 00:15:30.375
But I'll be fine.

244
00:15:30.458 --> 00:15:31.791
I'm sure, but...

245
00:15:38.041 --> 00:15:38.875
But what?

246
00:15:39.375 --> 00:15:40.666
It's not easy, dude.

247
00:15:41.541 --> 00:15:43.000
Getting over it, I mean.

248
00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:48.958
But she already did it.

249
00:15:49.833 --> 00:15:51.375
She is living her life.

250
00:15:53.541 --> 00:15:54.875
She suddenly cut me out.

251
00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.125
What am I waiting for?

252
00:16:04.833 --> 00:16:06.125
I won't wait either.

253
00:16:07.875 --> 00:16:09.208
I'll live my own life, dude.

254
00:16:09.291 --> 00:16:10.291
Easy now.

255
00:16:11.041 --> 00:16:12.583
Watch me get over her.

256
00:16:15.625 --> 00:16:16.500
Hi.

257
00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:19.333
Hi.

258
00:16:20.791 --> 00:16:23.958
I thought my order of <i>kunafa</i> arrived,
so I'm surprised to see you.

259
00:16:24.041 --> 00:16:24.875
Come on in.

260
00:16:36.833 --> 00:16:38.041
It was a good concert.

261
00:16:38.125 --> 00:16:39.708
Yeah, it was great.

262
00:16:40.791 --> 00:16:41.666
It was good.

263
00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.291
Nazım passed out immediately.

264
00:16:43.375 --> 00:16:45.958
That dumbass only cares about
having fun, not music.

265
00:16:47.958 --> 00:16:50.375
But you were really sweet, Mr. Semih.

266
00:16:50.458 --> 00:16:52.833
Thank you. Right back at you.

267
00:16:54.041 --> 00:16:55.708
I thought you'd kiss me again.

268
00:16:56.208 --> 00:16:57.083
What?

269
00:16:58.416 --> 00:16:59.541
Really? You...

270
00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.458
May I ask why <i>you</i> didn't kiss me?

271
00:17:05.666 --> 00:17:07.666
Oh, sorry. I forgot.

272
00:17:09.208 --> 00:17:11.125
You don't want a relationship.

273
00:17:13.916 --> 00:17:15.375
I want to be happy.

274
00:17:16.416 --> 00:17:17.541
Can we do that?

275
00:17:18.875 --> 00:17:19.791
We should try.

276
00:17:21.333 --> 00:17:22.166
Let's try.

277
00:17:41.458 --> 00:17:42.291
What?

278
00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:47.208
- Either red or white wine is fine.
- Coming right up!

279
00:17:47.291 --> 00:17:48.500
Bring whatever you have.

280
00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:01.083
A BIT WEIRD

281
00:18:01.166 --> 00:18:03.625
It's to remind you
of your first impression of me.

282
00:18:07.833 --> 00:18:09.666
You can say it's why I'm here.

283
00:18:14.041 --> 00:18:15.333
What are you thinking about?

284
00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:18.583
Nothing.

285
00:18:20.166 --> 00:18:21.041
Impossible.

286
00:18:22.125 --> 00:18:24.625
The world record for not thinking is
three seconds.

287
00:18:30.791 --> 00:18:32.125
How did they time it?

288
00:18:33.083 --> 00:18:35.041
With a stopwatch, I guess.

289
00:18:44.291 --> 00:18:45.166
Okay.

290
00:18:48.625 --> 00:18:50.666
I was told to take it slow, but...

291
00:18:54.125 --> 00:18:55.875
I think this counts as our second day.

292
00:18:56.375 --> 00:18:57.333
It's long enough.

293
00:19:32.875 --> 00:19:33.708
Seksek.

294
00:19:35.041 --> 00:19:36.458
You know what you should do?

295
00:19:37.208 --> 00:19:39.541
You know how they say,
"Think before you move"?

296
00:19:40.083 --> 00:19:42.666
But I really think
it should be in reverse order.

297
00:19:43.375 --> 00:19:45.500
You should move first.
You can think later.

298
00:19:53.833 --> 00:19:56.375
By the way, like hell you'll get over her.

299
00:19:56.916 --> 00:19:58.875
I know a thing or two about this stuff.

300
00:20:47.958 --> 00:20:52.375
I NEED A HOUSE LIKE THIS!
SEMİH

301
00:21:18.208 --> 00:21:20.208
SİBEL YÜKSEL HAIR SALON

302
00:21:28.583 --> 00:21:33.583
Wow! Believe it or not,
I have a friend who looks just like you!

303
00:21:33.666 --> 00:21:34.916
Is he just a friend?

304
00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:39.958
That's what he preferred to be back then,
and I respected that.

305
00:21:40.041 --> 00:21:41.875
What's your relationship now?

306
00:21:43.333 --> 00:21:44.708
I won't be your rebound.

307
00:21:44.791 --> 00:21:46.708
I didn't say anything. I just want coffee.

308
00:21:46.791 --> 00:21:50.625
Fine. There is a patio.
You can sit there if you want.

309
00:21:50.708 --> 00:21:51.625
Wow.

310
00:21:52.625 --> 00:21:54.708
So you got a loan to live your dreams?

311
00:21:54.791 --> 00:21:57.583
Yeah. I don't really earn much yet, but...

312
00:21:58.708 --> 00:22:00.416
I'm trying. I'm working hard.

313
00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:02.458
Turns out
you need to work hard to succeed.

314
00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.666
What is Akrasia? Is it like a tree?

315
00:22:07.416 --> 00:22:09.000
It sounds like a tree, right?

316
00:22:10.375 --> 00:22:11.666
It means weak-willed.

317
00:22:12.833 --> 00:22:14.500
I feel nervous.

318
00:22:16.875 --> 00:22:18.041
Firsts matter.

319
00:22:19.708 --> 00:22:22.541
- Come here.
- Semih...

320
00:22:28.625 --> 00:22:29.833
When did you... How...

321
00:22:30.458 --> 00:22:32.625
How did you make it? But...

322
00:22:34.166 --> 00:22:36.041
I can't believe it. What's happening?

323
00:22:36.125 --> 00:22:37.125
Look.

324
00:22:37.833 --> 00:22:39.125
Why don't you move in?

325
00:22:39.625 --> 00:22:41.166
It's closer to your workplace.

326
00:22:44.041 --> 00:22:47.375
- You'll get over it when you move?
- There is nothing to get over.

327
00:22:51.708 --> 00:22:53.875
What happens
if you get back together tomorrow?

328
00:22:53.958 --> 00:22:55.916
She'll come to find an empty apartment.

329
00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:58.083
We're talking about six years.

330
00:22:58.583 --> 00:23:00.666
There has to be some damages and losses.

331
00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:03.125
So you talk like a shopkeeper now?

332
00:23:04.500 --> 00:23:08.666
By the way, you are truly a mess
with those bandages and everything.

333
00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:12.166
Apart from your hair.
I love it. I'm obsessed.

334
00:23:13.833 --> 00:23:16.833
Why don't you find different interests?
Field hockey?

335
00:23:16.916 --> 00:23:18.000
Horse racing!

336
00:23:18.083 --> 00:23:19.458
Think about it.

337
00:23:26.291 --> 00:23:28.041
- Hey, man.
- Hey.

338
00:23:28.125 --> 00:23:29.416
When's the meeting, baby?

339
00:23:30.416 --> 00:23:31.250
What's going on?

340
00:23:31.958 --> 00:23:33.916
Let's see what you talk about
every morning.

341
00:23:34.000 --> 00:23:36.000
Dude, what's up with your hair?

342
00:23:36.875 --> 00:23:38.458
New is always interesting.

343
00:23:38.541 --> 00:23:42.750
So instead of turning to old stuff,
we just do new things.

344
00:23:42.833 --> 00:23:44.333
We aren't tied to the past.

345
00:23:44.833 --> 00:23:45.833
This is so pretty.

346
00:23:47.208 --> 00:23:48.041
Thanks.

347
00:23:48.833 --> 00:23:50.166
Where did you get it?

348
00:23:50.250 --> 00:23:52.708
It's really old, Ms. Ceyda.
I don't remember.

349
00:23:52.791 --> 00:23:53.958
Pretty. I like it.

350
00:23:54.041 --> 00:23:55.958
So you want us to go and tell this guy

351
00:23:56.041 --> 00:24:00.083
that he is incompetent
and he doesn't know shit.

352
00:24:00.166 --> 00:24:01.708
We should say it to his face?

353
00:24:01.791 --> 00:24:03.875
Not like that,
but we should say it somehow...

354
00:24:03.958 --> 00:24:05.333
Yes, we should.

355
00:24:05.416 --> 00:24:09.291
And I've been asking
how we can tell him all along. We need...

356
00:24:09.375 --> 00:24:10.458
Let me see that.

357
00:24:10.541 --> 00:24:12.416
What happened to your hand?
You're always hurt.

358
00:24:12.500 --> 00:24:14.416
Just a small accident, Ms. Ceyda.

359
00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:15.750
We need stuff like this.

360
00:24:16.791 --> 00:24:19.500
Why are you waiting?
Are you here for show, Semih?

361
00:24:19.583 --> 00:24:22.125
- Sorry, I don't understand.
- Can you improve it?

362
00:24:22.625 --> 00:24:23.458
Yeah...

363
00:24:23.541 --> 00:24:24.375
All right then.

364
00:24:24.458 --> 00:24:27.458
It should be like this.
It should have a story, a difference.

365
00:24:27.541 --> 00:24:29.958
This seems to be private.
Let's keep it private.

366
00:24:30.041 --> 00:24:33.791
We want it to have
some flavor, soul, and originality.

367
00:24:35.083 --> 00:24:38.000
If I come, I won't be able to
stay for long anyway. Yeah.

368
00:24:39.083 --> 00:24:42.083
And anyway, like you said. Okay.

369
00:24:42.833 --> 00:24:44.000
We'll talk later.

370
00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:46.916
Bye, dude. Bye.

371
00:24:47.958 --> 00:24:48.833
"Anyway"?

372
00:24:49.625 --> 00:24:52.416
Does it mean
"Anyway, Defne won't be able to come"?

373
00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:54.250
Yeah. Isn't it true?

374
00:24:54.833 --> 00:24:56.583
He keeps inviting us over.

375
00:24:57.166 --> 00:24:59.666
- Now...
- Now he can blame Defne.

376
00:24:59.750 --> 00:25:02.000
Have I ever said that, for God's sake?

377
00:25:02.083 --> 00:25:04.500
- I don't want to go either.
- Say it then.

378
00:25:04.583 --> 00:25:07.125
- Say what?
- Say, "I don't want to see you, bro."

379
00:25:08.250 --> 00:25:10.125
- But let me tell you something.
- Okay.

380
00:25:10.208 --> 00:25:11.166
You look fire.

381
00:25:11.916 --> 00:25:13.916
This suits you well. I made a good call.

382
00:25:14.000 --> 00:25:15.750
- Oh, really?
- Really.

383
00:25:15.833 --> 00:25:18.083
Should we have a little quickie in there?

384
00:25:19.541 --> 00:25:20.625
We'll be late.

385
00:25:21.208 --> 00:25:22.833
So, you think this is it?

386
00:25:23.583 --> 00:25:25.833
Look, let's take this off.

387
00:25:27.791 --> 00:25:29.125
Okay? That's step one.

388
00:25:29.708 --> 00:25:32.875
We can even get rid of these.

389
00:25:34.375 --> 00:25:35.833
Let's put these on.

390
00:25:38.041 --> 00:25:38.875
Look.

391
00:25:39.375 --> 00:25:40.208
Okay?

392
00:25:41.083 --> 00:25:42.875
This is it. We got it. Okay?

393
00:25:43.625 --> 00:25:44.833
Semih...

394
00:25:46.666 --> 00:25:48.875
So are you throwing all of these away?

395
00:25:48.958 --> 00:25:51.916
I'm not. Don't be silly.
We'll go through them together.

396
00:25:52.541 --> 00:25:53.541
Let's do it then.

397
00:25:58.375 --> 00:25:59.208
Semih!

398
00:26:07.125 --> 00:26:08.333
Come here!

399
00:26:13.791 --> 00:26:15.666
You see, this is the new me.

400
00:26:16.166 --> 00:26:18.208
Really? All right.

401
00:26:18.291 --> 00:26:19.375
We'll be late, come on!

402
00:26:23.125 --> 00:26:24.250
Should I come out?

403
00:26:28.458 --> 00:26:29.875
Should I come out like this?

404
00:26:31.458 --> 00:26:32.458
Kinky!

405
00:26:35.666 --> 00:26:36.750
What do you think?

406
00:26:44.208 --> 00:26:45.208
I'm ready too.

407
00:26:54.000 --> 00:26:56.791
Sorry for throwing your clothes away
without asking you.

408
00:26:57.333 --> 00:27:00.666
We let the whole neighborhood see us naked
just for a quickie.

409
00:27:02.083 --> 00:27:03.708
- Good for you.
- Yeah?

410
00:27:26.083 --> 00:27:27.333
How do you think it went?

411
00:27:28.250 --> 00:27:31.833
I mean, normal. Boring.

412
00:27:33.541 --> 00:27:34.541
Like me?

413
00:27:35.125 --> 00:27:37.583
Have I ever said that?
Where is that coming from?

414
00:27:38.125 --> 00:27:39.291
I mean, it's...

415
00:27:40.458 --> 00:27:41.625
- Come here.
- That...

416
00:27:41.708 --> 00:27:44.041
- Come on!
- What are you doing?

417
00:27:44.125 --> 00:27:46.583
Sir, wait a second please!
Come here, baby.

418
00:27:46.666 --> 00:27:49.625
- What are you doing, Semih?
- Trust me. Let's go!

419
00:27:49.708 --> 00:27:51.250
- We're coming!
- Semih.

420
00:27:53.666 --> 00:27:54.666
What is happening?

421
00:27:55.625 --> 00:27:57.541
We don't know where this bus is going.

422
00:27:58.375 --> 00:27:59.250
So?

423
00:28:01.416 --> 00:28:03.375
Don't you want to see where it ends up?

424
00:28:04.541 --> 00:28:05.375
So?

425
00:28:07.958 --> 00:28:08.791
Yes.

426
00:28:45.833 --> 00:28:46.666
Defne?

427
00:28:49.083 --> 00:28:49.916
What's going on?

428
00:28:52.958 --> 00:28:54.083
I love you so much.

429
00:29:02.500 --> 00:29:03.458
Okay, go on.

430
00:29:04.375 --> 00:29:05.250
I'm listening.

431
00:29:08.291 --> 00:29:09.125
I was always...

432
00:29:13.166 --> 00:29:15.250
Deep down, I was always sad, you know?

433
00:29:17.125 --> 00:29:19.000
- I had an inkling.
- No.

434
00:29:20.875 --> 00:29:22.458
You've never seen me like that.

435
00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:28.083
It was really dark.

436
00:29:31.041 --> 00:29:33.041
Nobody would understand.

437
00:29:35.541 --> 00:29:36.791
And what happened?

438
00:29:39.916 --> 00:29:40.791
It's gone now.

439
00:29:44.166 --> 00:29:45.666
You've helped me forget it.

440
00:29:54.041 --> 00:29:54.875
You silly...

441
00:30:01.541 --> 00:30:02.958
All right.

442
00:30:03.041 --> 00:30:04.625
Let's get back to work.

443
00:30:05.125 --> 00:30:06.458
The meeting is over.

444
00:30:15.041 --> 00:30:16.791
- Ms. Ceyda!
- All right...

445
00:30:16.875 --> 00:30:17.750
Ms. Ceyda!

446
00:30:18.416 --> 00:30:20.375
- I can improve it.
- Improve what, dear?

447
00:30:21.458 --> 00:30:23.458
You asked if I could improve it.

448
00:30:23.541 --> 00:30:26.000
Do it, obviously.
That's what we expect from you.

449
00:30:26.083 --> 00:30:28.125
We've been expecting it for a while,
right, Semih?

450
00:30:47.416 --> 00:30:50.333
- I guess she wanted to get married.
- Is that what she told you?

451
00:30:50.416 --> 00:30:52.791
- Who?
- Defne. You said you spoke to her.

452
00:30:52.875 --> 00:30:55.333
She didn't tell me that.
It's just what normally happens.

453
00:30:55.416 --> 00:30:58.958
They want marriage. It doesn't happen.
You break up. Isn't it what happened?

454
00:30:59.041 --> 00:31:01.416
We never talked about it.
It never came up.

455
00:31:02.166 --> 00:31:04.541
I bet it happened,
but you didn't talk about it.

456
00:31:05.250 --> 00:31:07.458
What did Defne tell you exactly?

457
00:31:08.500 --> 00:31:10.208
She said you weren't happy anyway.

458
00:31:11.041 --> 00:31:12.125
She said "anyway"?

459
00:31:13.125 --> 00:31:14.375
She did, but...

460
00:31:15.125 --> 00:31:19.125
I mean, it's now... Anyway, right?

461
00:31:19.208 --> 00:31:20.875
Yes, exactly.

462
00:31:21.750 --> 00:31:22.750
Look.

463
00:31:23.875 --> 00:31:24.916
You aren't upset, right?

464
00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.708
Of course not. I'm really...
That would be childish.

465
00:31:28.333 --> 00:31:29.416
Don't bottle it up.

466
00:31:30.875 --> 00:31:32.208
Give yourself some time.

467
00:31:32.708 --> 00:31:34.958
Yes. I have my hands full anyway.

468
00:31:36.583 --> 00:31:39.541
- By the way, I'm moving to a new place.
- Oh, that's great.

469
00:31:39.625 --> 00:31:42.041
- So you're over it?
- Of course.

470
00:31:42.666 --> 00:31:45.166
That's good to hear
because that's how Defne feels too.

471
00:31:45.250 --> 00:31:49.125
I didn't know your mental state
or if you were in the mood to party.

472
00:31:49.208 --> 00:31:50.208
Why didn't you say so?

473
00:31:51.625 --> 00:31:53.291
Defne is in the mood to party?

474
00:31:53.375 --> 00:31:54.875
I got that vibe.

475
00:31:54.958 --> 00:31:57.375
In fact,
she was supposed to be here today.

476
00:31:58.208 --> 00:31:59.958
I guess she didn't come
knowing you'd be here.

477
00:32:00.041 --> 00:32:03.500
Let me give you a hug. Aw, poor baby!

478
00:32:03.583 --> 00:32:05.875
You didn't tell me about Defne.

479
00:32:05.958 --> 00:32:07.041
Are you okay?

480
00:32:07.125 --> 00:32:08.791
I'm okay. I'm all good.

481
00:32:08.875 --> 00:32:10.125
Okay, awesome.

482
00:32:10.208 --> 00:32:11.583
The customer took the deal.

483
00:32:11.666 --> 00:32:13.166
- Finally.
- Great.

484
00:32:13.250 --> 00:32:15.666
- They are even asking about the deadline.
- Great.

485
00:32:16.208 --> 00:32:18.708
- I'm telling you. Do you understand?
- Of course.

486
00:32:18.791 --> 00:32:22.583
Okay. You'll see him kill it
after all this time, my love.

487
00:32:22.666 --> 00:32:24.125
It's been a really long time.

488
00:32:25.416 --> 00:32:27.291
You really took your time, Semih!

489
00:32:27.875 --> 00:32:30.916
Don't say that!
We knew he was trying to adjust.

490
00:32:31.000 --> 00:32:33.833
- But we didn't know it would take so long.
- Okay, enough about work.

491
00:32:33.916 --> 00:32:35.208
Come here. Look.

492
00:32:35.291 --> 00:32:39.000
Don't try to ditch work saying you have
an ingrown hair or a headache. Don't!

493
00:32:39.083 --> 00:32:40.750
- This job is different.
- Don't worry.

494
00:32:40.833 --> 00:32:43.416
- Let me know if you won't do it.
- Don't worry. I got it.

495
00:32:43.500 --> 00:32:44.750
Okay then.

496
00:32:44.833 --> 00:32:47.125
- Love, Tansu is leaving with his partner.
- Yeah? I'm coming.

497
00:32:47.208 --> 00:32:49.875
- Do you understand?
- I got it. Don't worry. I'm on it.

498
00:33:13.958 --> 00:33:14.791
Stop.

499
00:33:18.250 --> 00:33:19.166
Stop.

500
00:33:21.208 --> 00:33:22.208
Semih...

501
00:33:23.875 --> 00:33:24.708
Stop.

502
00:33:29.458 --> 00:33:31.458
Stop. It'll be a scandal.

503
00:33:31.958 --> 00:33:32.833
Stop.

504
00:33:37.833 --> 00:33:38.791
You go first.

505
00:34:34.125 --> 00:34:35.541
You were doing great!

506
00:34:36.041 --> 00:34:38.333
- When did you get here?
- To the recital?

507
00:34:39.083 --> 00:34:40.791
Please, I can't play it at all.

508
00:34:40.875 --> 00:34:44.250
- I'm only trying because it's your gift.
- But it sounds great.

509
00:34:44.333 --> 00:34:45.833
Don't come in with your shoes.

510
00:34:48.458 --> 00:34:50.541
Hours of YouTube gave me a headache.

511
00:34:50.625 --> 00:34:51.666
But that's great.

512
00:34:52.333 --> 00:34:54.458
Why don't you quit your job
and focus on music?

513
00:34:54.541 --> 00:34:56.500
You should focus on the ukulele we bought.

514
00:34:56.583 --> 00:34:59.250
It feels a little small.
Maybe we should get a bigger one?

515
00:34:59.333 --> 00:35:01.041
You never make an effort.

516
00:35:01.125 --> 00:35:04.000
It's because I hated my music teacher
back in primary school.

517
00:35:05.125 --> 00:35:06.583
Don't drink from the bottle!

518
00:35:07.541 --> 00:35:09.333
And refill it, please.

519
00:35:14.333 --> 00:35:15.500
Where are my clothes?

520
00:35:20.291 --> 00:35:21.916
I'm so sorry. Fuck, I forgot.

521
00:35:22.000 --> 00:35:24.166
I asked for a single favor, Semih.

522
00:35:24.250 --> 00:35:26.958
I know. You said you needed them
for the meeting.

523
00:35:28.250 --> 00:35:30.125
There you go!

524
00:35:30.208 --> 00:35:31.041
What?

525
00:35:31.541 --> 00:35:32.500
Fuck.

526
00:35:33.000 --> 00:35:33.833
Semih...

527
00:35:35.000 --> 00:35:38.875
Wait, I'll figure it out.
I bet they have a number here somewhere.

528
00:35:38.958 --> 00:35:41.625
- How will you figure it out?
- I will, baby. Just wait.

529
00:35:44.583 --> 00:35:46.166
- Okay...
- I'm going home, Semih.

530
00:35:46.250 --> 00:35:48.375
- Wait, don't go. Wait, please.
- I'm going home.

531
00:35:50.083 --> 00:35:56.875
LEVENT DRY CLEANING

532
00:36:01.583 --> 00:36:04.250
FOR SALE - HANDE SEVCEN
SEVCEN REAL ESTATE SERVICES

533
00:36:50.583 --> 00:36:53.291
I'm waiting for you to clean that window.

534
00:36:54.500 --> 00:36:56.791
- If you could reply to my messages...
- What?

535
00:36:56.875 --> 00:36:59.500
I called you, Mr. Semih.
You declined my call.

536
00:37:00.458 --> 00:37:01.791
That's impossible.

537
00:37:03.166 --> 00:37:06.291
Unbelievable. You look so sure.
I'm about to question myself.

538
00:37:07.083 --> 00:37:08.250
If you say so...

539
00:37:08.333 --> 00:37:12.041
I called you twice.
Then I thought it was another false alarm.

540
00:37:12.125 --> 00:37:15.333
I decided to wait because I felt like
I was forcing you to move out.

541
00:37:15.416 --> 00:37:17.000
I'm guilty of having done that.

542
00:37:18.250 --> 00:37:20.958
But you aren't looking for a place, right?

543
00:37:21.041 --> 00:37:23.958
I am. I need a place right now.

544
00:37:24.041 --> 00:37:27.208
Then you should look for it online
by yourself.

545
00:37:29.416 --> 00:37:30.791
What if I say sorry?

546
00:37:31.333 --> 00:37:33.625
I'm not going to chase after you.

547
00:37:33.708 --> 00:37:37.416
This is weird, isn't it?
It's as if I'm forcing you or something.

548
00:37:37.500 --> 00:37:39.375
That's not the case at all.

549
00:37:39.458 --> 00:37:42.208
Anyway, you know what?

550
00:37:42.291 --> 00:37:45.541
I don't think
you are looking for a new place.

551
00:37:45.625 --> 00:37:48.583
That's what you said on day one. Right?

552
00:37:49.166 --> 00:37:50.375
Have fun swimming.

553
00:37:52.833 --> 00:37:53.916
Nice ass.

554
00:37:54.916 --> 00:37:57.375
Nice ass. You've got to hand it to her.

555
00:37:58.625 --> 00:38:00.083
I can set you up if you want.

556
00:38:00.583 --> 00:38:01.708
You can't pull it off.

557
00:38:02.750 --> 00:38:03.750
Come here.

558
00:38:10.333 --> 00:38:11.416
Def!

559
00:38:12.166 --> 00:38:13.000
Def!

560
00:38:15.166 --> 00:38:16.166
Fuck.

561
00:38:18.708 --> 00:38:19.875
Excuse me.

562
00:38:19.958 --> 00:38:22.291
- My boyfriend loves tattoos.
- Oh?

563
00:38:23.166 --> 00:38:25.458
Your tattoo blew his mind.

564
00:38:25.541 --> 00:38:28.250
Is it okay if he takes a closer look?

565
00:38:33.041 --> 00:38:34.041
Def...

566
00:38:34.750 --> 00:38:37.916
Look, your jealousy is
completely uncalled-for right now.

567
00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:40.333
Who decides
whether it is uncalled-for or not?

568
00:38:40.416 --> 00:38:41.625
This is so lame.

569
00:38:41.708 --> 00:38:43.750
What's lame, Semih?

570
00:38:44.416 --> 00:38:45.833
This whole jealousy thing.

571
00:38:47.500 --> 00:38:49.833
Maybe it's lame for you
to be with somebody, Semih.

572
00:38:49.916 --> 00:38:51.875
- Def...
- Maybe I'm lame.

573
00:38:51.958 --> 00:38:53.958
You're not. I'm just a bit weird.

574
00:38:55.208 --> 00:38:56.916
- Def!
- Fine.

575
00:38:58.916 --> 00:39:00.916
Coming out here was a great idea, right?

576
00:39:05.000 --> 00:39:06.875
But I already told you what I think.

577
00:39:06.958 --> 00:39:08.208
I didn't want a baby.

578
00:39:08.291 --> 00:39:10.083
But you tried to broach the subject.

579
00:39:10.166 --> 00:39:12.125
I didn't. My friend had a baby.

580
00:39:12.791 --> 00:39:14.166
Am I not allowed to say it?

581
00:39:15.416 --> 00:39:17.458
Plus, if I wanted a baby,
I wouldn't have it with you.

582
00:39:17.541 --> 00:39:18.625
I mean...

583
00:39:19.291 --> 00:39:21.666
True, we would need to have sex first.

584
00:39:21.750 --> 00:39:23.291
I have to fricking work!

585
00:39:23.375 --> 00:39:25.833
I can't do whatever I want like you.

586
00:39:27.541 --> 00:39:30.000
You always need to have
something going on, right?

587
00:39:31.125 --> 00:39:33.083
You can't sit still for a moment.

588
00:39:34.208 --> 00:39:35.291
Keep rowing.

589
00:39:35.916 --> 00:39:37.750
No, let's sit still.

590
00:39:38.541 --> 00:39:40.958
Let's see what it's like to not move.

591
00:39:48.041 --> 00:39:49.000
What are you doing?

592
00:39:51.666 --> 00:39:52.666
Come on then.

593
00:39:54.125 --> 00:39:55.000
Come here!

594
00:41:15.750 --> 00:41:18.958
Yes, I know it's not complete yet.
There is more to be done.

595
00:41:22.375 --> 00:41:23.208
Yes.

596
00:41:24.041 --> 00:41:25.125
This is not like us.

597
00:41:25.208 --> 00:41:26.875
I thought you had something to show me.

598
00:41:26.958 --> 00:41:30.166
- But I'm trying. I'm searching.
- Sometimes trying is not enough, right?

599
00:41:31.291 --> 00:41:33.916
- Do what you want, but this is not it.
- Okay.

600
00:41:36.791 --> 00:41:39.000
- May I ask you something, Ms. Ceyda?
- Do it fast.

601
00:41:39.083 --> 00:41:41.583
Could you give me an advance if possible?

602
00:41:41.666 --> 00:41:43.833
An advance? You just got paid.

603
00:41:43.916 --> 00:41:48.166
I know, but it's about my rent.
I'm moving out, and my landlord...

604
00:41:50.916 --> 00:41:52.041
Hello?

605
00:41:52.125 --> 00:41:53.583
Semih will visit you, İsmail.

606
00:41:53.666 --> 00:41:55.958
Pay him an advance for the new job.

607
00:41:58.708 --> 00:42:00.750
I think you're supposed to thank me.

608
00:42:00.833 --> 00:42:02.208
Thank you so much. Thanks.

609
00:42:02.291 --> 00:42:05.125
It's coming out of your commission,
or if you don't work, your salary.

610
00:42:05.208 --> 00:42:07.583
- Obviously. I got it.
- You got it.

611
00:42:08.166 --> 00:42:09.000
I got it.

612
00:42:10.125 --> 00:42:11.083
For God's sake.

613
00:42:19.375 --> 00:42:23.583
I had the audacity to tell the guy
he never emailed us about delivering work.

614
00:42:23.666 --> 00:42:25.750
And he said, "I did, Ms. Ceyda."

615
00:42:25.833 --> 00:42:28.625
What's your problem, Özge?
Where is your mind?

616
00:42:31.041 --> 00:42:35.750
- I swear I didn't receive it, Ms. Ceyda.
- I'm sick of these mistakes, Özge.

617
00:42:35.833 --> 00:42:38.000
I told the guy we never got an email...

618
00:42:38.083 --> 00:42:39.125
Hello, love.

619
00:42:41.875 --> 00:42:43.541
You don't sound well. What happened?

620
00:42:45.583 --> 00:42:46.958
Oh no.

621
00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:50.166
No.

622
00:42:52.291 --> 00:42:56.583
Oh, my love. Yes, I know. Of course I do.

623
00:42:57.791 --> 00:42:58.958
I can imagine.

624
00:43:00.333 --> 00:43:01.375
Don't cry.

625
00:43:04.958 --> 00:43:06.166
My condolences.

626
00:43:07.666 --> 00:43:09.583
Okay.

627
00:43:10.916 --> 00:43:13.166
I know. My poor baby. I know.

628
00:43:13.250 --> 00:43:15.541
- Tell me something.
- I'm sorry.

629
00:43:15.625 --> 00:43:16.458
Okay.

630
00:43:16.541 --> 00:43:17.750
It's all good then!

631
00:43:18.750 --> 00:43:22.166
Listen to me. Don't cry. Please listen.

632
00:43:23.458 --> 00:43:25.625
Ceyda is holding a meeting right now.

633
00:43:26.416 --> 00:43:28.166
I have to go, okay?

634
00:43:30.791 --> 00:43:33.291
I'll come if I can get out of it,
all right?

635
00:43:34.583 --> 00:43:36.083
Okay.

636
00:43:36.166 --> 00:43:37.583
I love you too. Bye.

637
00:43:39.208 --> 00:43:40.375
What meeting?

638
00:43:42.416 --> 00:43:44.125
Don't we have a meeting?

639
00:43:45.208 --> 00:43:47.083
As if you join our meetings.

640
00:43:50.083 --> 00:43:51.541
Def's grandma passed away.

641
00:43:53.416 --> 00:43:55.083
- My condolences.
- Yeah.

642
00:43:57.208 --> 00:43:58.875
But I'm not good with this stuff.

643
00:43:59.958 --> 00:44:00.958
What stuff?

644
00:44:01.500 --> 00:44:03.625
This stuff. Funerals and everything.

645
00:44:04.708 --> 00:44:07.083
Crying and all that stuff.

646
00:44:07.583 --> 00:44:09.208
I can't deal with all that.

647
00:44:09.291 --> 00:44:10.833
But it's part of life.

648
00:44:13.583 --> 00:44:14.666
What happened to you?

649
00:44:16.041 --> 00:44:17.125
Same old, same old.

650
00:44:17.208 --> 00:44:19.166
I want to get the fuck away from here.

651
00:44:19.250 --> 00:44:21.208
Ceyda ripped me a new hole.

652
00:44:21.958 --> 00:44:23.375
I'm never good enough.

653
00:44:24.458 --> 00:44:26.750
Hey, what's going on?

654
00:44:26.833 --> 00:44:28.750
You'll sort it out. It's okay.

655
00:44:28.833 --> 00:44:30.500
She really berated me this time, Semih.

656
00:44:30.583 --> 00:44:32.625
She scolded me as if I was a kid.

657
00:44:32.708 --> 00:44:35.125
I know, but Ceyda is always like this.

658
00:44:35.208 --> 00:44:36.791
Don't mind her. What did Uğur say?

659
00:44:37.458 --> 00:44:40.458
He liked it,
but he is Ceyda's husband after all.

660
00:44:40.541 --> 00:44:43.708
What matters is he liked it.
Never mind Ceyda's usual crazy self.

661
00:44:44.375 --> 00:44:45.500
I'm so tired.

662
00:44:45.583 --> 00:44:48.291
You're working. You're bound to be tired.

663
00:44:49.041 --> 00:44:51.541
Make yourself some coffee
and get it together, okay?

664
00:44:53.500 --> 00:44:55.250
You're so weird.

665
00:44:55.333 --> 00:44:57.791
You're consoling me
when there is a funeral going on.

666
00:44:57.875 --> 00:45:00.416
Wipe your tears. Come on now.

667
00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:35.666
Are you still willing to help me?

668
00:45:39.500 --> 00:45:41.041
Pizza and wine on me. Tonight.

669
00:45:42.750 --> 00:45:45.375
Come on!
She'll eat me alive, don't you see?

670
00:45:45.875 --> 00:45:48.041
Come on!

671
00:45:48.125 --> 00:45:50.958
- Okay, I'll let my husband know.
- You're awesome.

672
00:45:51.041 --> 00:45:53.416
Here, keep the cotton branch.
I need to get this.

673
00:45:53.916 --> 00:45:54.791
Hello?

674
00:45:55.541 --> 00:45:57.791
I'm on my way, Mom. Don't panic.

675
00:45:57.875 --> 00:45:59.291
<i>He has arrived. He's waiting.</i>

676
00:45:59.375 --> 00:46:02.541
<i>Why didn't you leave earlier?
What if something happens to him?</i>

677
00:46:02.625 --> 00:46:05.000
He's a big boy. What could even happen?

678
00:46:05.083 --> 00:46:08.041
Why didn't you let me know beforehand?
How could I know when he'd land?

679
00:46:08.125 --> 00:46:09.375
<i>I texted you.</i>

680
00:46:09.458 --> 00:46:11.333
I told you, my phone is broken, Mom.

681
00:46:11.416 --> 00:46:12.666
<i>Get it fixed, then.</i>

682
00:46:12.750 --> 00:46:15.250
<i>Mr. Hüseyin called me
about your notice to vacate.</i>

683
00:46:15.333 --> 00:46:17.041
<i>Are you moving out? What happened?</i>

684
00:46:17.125 --> 00:46:19.000
What? Why is he calling you?

685
00:46:19.916 --> 00:46:21.416
<i>Because your phone is broken.</i>

686
00:46:22.541 --> 00:46:25.458
All right, I'll call you later, Mom. Okay?

687
00:46:25.541 --> 00:46:27.458
<i>Okay. Bye.</i>

688
00:46:33.416 --> 00:46:34.333
Hello.

689
00:46:38.458 --> 00:46:39.416
No way.

690
00:46:40.416 --> 00:46:41.875
You can't be serious.

691
00:46:43.208 --> 00:46:45.375
Def! What a coincidence!

692
00:46:46.125 --> 00:46:48.958
Hello, sir. I know this lady.
Could we please swap seats?

693
00:46:49.041 --> 00:46:51.791
No, please don't bother! I'm good.

694
00:46:51.875 --> 00:46:54.875
She is pretending to not know me.
Do you understand? Can I...

695
00:46:54.958 --> 00:46:57.500
- Excuse me, is there a problem?
- No, not at all.

696
00:46:57.583 --> 00:46:59.333
This lady keeps bothering me.

697
00:46:59.416 --> 00:47:02.625
I don't know what to do. I want to
sit here, but she insists I sit with her.

698
00:47:02.708 --> 00:47:03.916
I like the aisle seat.

699
00:47:24.291 --> 00:47:26.583
I want to see Kars, so I'm going there.

700
00:47:29.625 --> 00:47:33.041
I'm sick of all this weird stuff, okay?
You don't think about me.

701
00:47:33.125 --> 00:47:35.041
I'm here because I think about you.

702
00:47:35.125 --> 00:47:37.125
Interesting, don't you have a meeting?

703
00:47:38.416 --> 00:47:41.041
I know, but Ceyda stressed us out, okay?

704
00:47:41.125 --> 00:47:43.916
I know it's ridiculous,
but I couldn't get out of work. Okay?

705
00:47:44.000 --> 00:47:46.333
I couldn't come to the funeral.
I'm really sorry.

706
00:47:46.416 --> 00:47:48.916
- I wish I could've been there.
- I wish you weren't here.

707
00:47:51.500 --> 00:47:54.166
You know that I know
you don't like seminars.

708
00:47:54.666 --> 00:47:55.833
I'll be fine.

709
00:47:55.916 --> 00:47:56.833
Without you.

710
00:47:56.916 --> 00:48:00.375
Is that so? Without me? Watch this.

711
00:48:00.458 --> 00:48:02.708
I swear I'll crash this plane!
Where is that red handle?

712
00:48:02.791 --> 00:48:05.000
I'll crash this plane and end it all!

713
00:48:05.083 --> 00:48:06.791
I'll kill us all! Do you hear me?

714
00:48:06.875 --> 00:48:08.500
I'm kidding.

715
00:48:09.625 --> 00:48:11.625
We're trying to resolve a problem.

716
00:48:12.250 --> 00:48:13.083
Sorry.

717
00:48:14.458 --> 00:48:15.625
We are almost there.

718
00:48:15.708 --> 00:48:16.708
See you in Kars.

719
00:48:18.458 --> 00:48:19.291
Look.

720
00:48:20.375 --> 00:48:22.875
Don't disturb me today, okay?

721
00:48:24.208 --> 00:48:26.375
Don't show up. Don't call.

722
00:48:26.458 --> 00:48:28.291
Don't do ridiculous stuff.

723
00:48:29.666 --> 00:48:32.041
Don't try to pull something off, okay?

724
00:48:32.666 --> 00:48:33.791
Do you hear me?

725
00:48:35.041 --> 00:48:36.083
I can't focus!

726
00:48:39.875 --> 00:48:41.041
Don't worry about me.

727
00:48:43.333 --> 00:48:45.000
Does your company cover the minibar?

728
00:48:47.375 --> 00:48:49.166
- Welcome.
- Hello.

729
00:48:57.208 --> 00:48:59.250
- Can I get a whiskey?
- Right away.

730
00:48:59.333 --> 00:49:01.041
- Thanks.
- Enjoy.

731
00:49:01.125 --> 00:49:02.041
Thank you.

732
00:49:09.208 --> 00:49:10.833
- Can I get another?
- Right away.

733
00:49:28.041 --> 00:49:28.916
Nice tattoo.

734
00:49:32.125 --> 00:49:33.125
My handiwork.

735
00:49:33.666 --> 00:49:34.541
Wow.

736
00:49:35.416 --> 00:49:36.583
Thanks.

737
00:49:41.375 --> 00:49:42.750
What are you doing here?

738
00:49:45.541 --> 00:49:46.541
What I need to do.

739
00:49:47.291 --> 00:49:48.166
Really?

740
00:49:50.000 --> 00:49:51.291
What do you need to do?

741
00:49:54.166 --> 00:49:57.458
My girlfriend is here for a seminar,
and I'm here with her.

742
00:49:57.958 --> 00:50:01.916
To do what? Support her mentally?

743
00:50:03.125 --> 00:50:04.458
Can I get a napkin?

744
00:50:05.541 --> 00:50:06.958
I just love Kars.

745
00:50:07.041 --> 00:50:10.083
Really? What do you love
the most about it?

746
00:50:11.166 --> 00:50:12.000
It's cold.

747
00:50:12.750 --> 00:50:14.250
But it's a beautiful city.

748
00:50:16.875 --> 00:50:19.083
Why aren't you in the seminar?

749
00:50:20.833 --> 00:50:22.500
I'm here as a matter of form.

750
00:50:22.583 --> 00:50:23.958
My dad insisted on it.

751
00:50:24.541 --> 00:50:25.875
Is he the general manager?

752
00:50:25.958 --> 00:50:31.125
Kind of, yeah.
Our family has a corporate background.

753
00:50:31.208 --> 00:50:34.375
- Okay.
- And they think there is hope for me.

754
00:50:35.833 --> 00:50:36.750
And is there?

755
00:50:37.875 --> 00:50:40.416
Where there's life,
there's hope, of course.

756
00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:43.250
But seminars are not for me.

757
00:50:44.625 --> 00:50:46.416
What kind of place do you have in mind?

758
00:50:49.083 --> 00:50:50.458
A place that is mine.

759
00:50:52.041 --> 00:50:55.375
So I should be able to afford it.

760
00:50:57.625 --> 00:51:00.333
I just want to serve
some good coffee, some snacks,

761
00:51:00.416 --> 00:51:02.791
and in the afternoon, a few cocktails.

762
00:51:03.541 --> 00:51:04.375
Cool.

763
00:51:05.791 --> 00:51:06.625
I'll visit.

764
00:51:07.583 --> 00:51:08.541
Please do.

765
00:51:13.291 --> 00:51:15.291
Don't you ever get sick of yourself?

766
00:51:17.875 --> 00:51:18.708
I don't know.

767
00:51:21.416 --> 00:51:22.583
I don't have time for it.

768
00:51:23.083 --> 00:51:24.291
So you're busy.

769
00:51:32.083 --> 00:51:33.125
Anyway...

770
00:51:37.750 --> 00:51:39.000
I'll get going.

771
00:51:40.958 --> 00:51:45.333
How about exchanging numbers?
Should we do it?

772
00:51:46.375 --> 00:51:47.500
Let me type it.

773
00:51:48.166 --> 00:51:49.166
You're so subtle.

774
00:51:52.166 --> 00:51:58.250
You can go back to your girlfriend
in your room without feeling any guilt.

775
00:51:58.333 --> 00:52:00.333
You haven't done anything wrong.

776
00:52:02.541 --> 00:52:07.958
But I'm going to need to forget about you.

777
00:52:08.041 --> 00:52:11.916
And I will take care of that by myself.

778
00:52:15.458 --> 00:52:16.375
I'm going now.

779
00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:17.833
Cool.

780
00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:24.166
- Good night.
- Good night.

781
00:52:35.541 --> 00:52:36.541
Good morning.

782
00:52:59.875 --> 00:53:01.250
The florists were closed.

783
00:53:01.333 --> 00:53:04.041
THE FLORISTS WERE CLOSED

784
00:53:12.291 --> 00:53:13.625
I'm really sorry.

785
00:53:17.375 --> 00:53:18.375
I apologize.

786
00:53:20.500 --> 00:53:21.916
Apologize to my grandma.

787
00:53:23.750 --> 00:53:26.500
She loved you. I don't know why.

788
00:53:29.958 --> 00:53:31.208
I finished up the tattoo.

789
00:53:31.791 --> 00:53:33.125
I won't get a tattoo.

790
00:53:33.208 --> 00:53:34.291
What do you mean?

791
00:53:35.791 --> 00:53:36.625
Look.

792
00:53:39.625 --> 00:53:40.458
Fish.

793
00:53:41.583 --> 00:53:43.708
Symbolizing all the Pisces in the family.

794
00:53:50.625 --> 00:53:52.625
Who is Beril, exactly?

795
00:53:53.166 --> 00:53:54.833
An old friend.

796
00:53:55.750 --> 00:53:57.166
Why don't I know her?

797
00:53:59.291 --> 00:54:01.166
Because I no longer talk to her.

798
00:54:03.291 --> 00:54:05.958
What if I received this text
from somebody I no longer talk to?

799
00:54:06.041 --> 00:54:07.208
What if I sent it?

800
00:54:11.375 --> 00:54:13.625
I guess I'd ask about that person, Def.

801
00:54:16.916 --> 00:54:19.333
"You're like a shop that's open 24/7."

802
00:54:20.208 --> 00:54:22.458
"But there's a line
whenever I come around."

803
00:54:23.083 --> 00:54:23.916
Huh.

804
00:54:26.500 --> 00:54:27.541
She is funny.

805
00:54:29.750 --> 00:54:31.000
So she isn't like me.

806
00:54:31.083 --> 00:54:33.750
Is that what I said, Defne?

807
00:54:35.125 --> 00:54:37.000
How will you reply to her?

808
00:54:39.416 --> 00:54:40.541
With a smiley face.

809
00:54:41.083 --> 00:54:42.083
With a smiley face?

810
00:54:42.833 --> 00:54:44.041
What else?

811
00:54:45.833 --> 00:54:47.125
I'm not done yet.

812
00:54:47.666 --> 00:54:48.666
So...

813
00:54:49.625 --> 00:54:51.666
So you want all the doors

814
00:54:52.791 --> 00:54:56.208
to be always open for you, right?

815
00:54:56.291 --> 00:54:59.625
And you want to hang out in the hallway.
That's your thing.

816
00:54:59.708 --> 00:55:02.208
- See, this is funny too.
- You're breaking my heart.

817
00:55:04.791 --> 00:55:05.833
Def!

818
00:55:08.375 --> 00:55:09.208
Cool.

819
00:55:14.791 --> 00:55:16.875
I got him, Mom. We're driving back, okay?

820
00:55:16.958 --> 00:55:18.750
<i>Okay, be careful.</i>

821
00:55:18.833 --> 00:55:21.583
<i>I sent you some tomato paste.
Give it to Defne, okay?</i>

822
00:55:21.666 --> 00:55:24.041
- See you, Mom.
- Fuck off with your tomato paste.

823
00:55:31.791 --> 00:55:32.958
How is it in Antalya?

824
00:55:34.291 --> 00:55:35.125
Hot.

825
00:55:36.208 --> 00:55:38.166
It's cold here. I was cold when we landed.

826
00:55:38.250 --> 00:55:39.083
Yeah.

827
00:55:40.375 --> 00:55:41.708
Isn't Defne here?

828
00:55:42.916 --> 00:55:45.083
Nope. We broke up.

829
00:55:45.791 --> 00:55:46.625
Why?

830
00:55:46.708 --> 00:55:48.875
You don't mind asking at all, you Gen Zer.

831
00:55:57.333 --> 00:55:58.875
It looks serious.

832
00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:00.833
What?

833
00:56:01.416 --> 00:56:02.666
Is she really mad at you?

834
00:56:02.750 --> 00:56:03.958
Tell me what's going on.

835
00:56:05.250 --> 00:56:07.791
She deleted all of your photos
from her profile.

836
00:56:12.541 --> 00:56:13.666
She deleted all of them?

837
00:56:14.166 --> 00:56:15.916
Yes, she did.

838
00:56:16.416 --> 00:56:18.500
But she doesn't have a bikini pic yet.

839
00:56:18.583 --> 00:56:19.916
What does that mean?

840
00:56:21.625 --> 00:56:24.041
Something like "I'm available."

841
00:56:26.875 --> 00:56:28.333
Get your luggage and let's go.

842
00:56:28.416 --> 00:56:29.250
Okay.

843
00:56:33.041 --> 00:56:34.208
I need to do something.

844
00:56:35.833 --> 00:56:37.208
How much does it cost?

845
00:56:37.916 --> 00:56:39.375
It'll be 900 for you.

846
00:56:39.458 --> 00:56:40.291
Whoa!

847
00:56:40.916 --> 00:56:43.041
Nine hundred? What does it normally cost?

848
00:56:43.125 --> 00:56:44.125
It's all imported.

849
00:56:44.625 --> 00:56:47.625
- I'll just pay more and get a new one...
- Here you go.

850
00:56:47.708 --> 00:56:50.208
- What are you doing, you nutcase?
- Mom sent it.

851
00:56:50.291 --> 00:56:52.916
- What the hell?
- Because you wouldn't get it fixed.

852
00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:54.166
Please, take it.

853
00:56:57.500 --> 00:56:59.625
Poyraz! Come on, I ordered us pizza.

854
00:57:01.833 --> 00:57:02.750
How much is it?

855
00:57:04.041 --> 00:57:06.375
It's okay. We can make a good deal.

856
00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:09.708
- Did you forget I was coming?
- Don't be silly. Come in.

857
00:57:10.291 --> 00:57:12.875
- Hello. Am I disturbing you?
- Not at all.

858
00:57:14.541 --> 00:57:16.750
He's been stuck for the past three years.

859
00:57:16.833 --> 00:57:18.958
It's better than going
to a university I don't want.

860
00:57:19.041 --> 00:57:22.250
- Fuck off. His dad takes care of him.
- He doesn't take care of you?

861
00:57:22.333 --> 00:57:25.541
My dad took care of himself.
His dad takes care of everyone.

862
00:57:25.625 --> 00:57:28.541
- We have different fathers.
- I didn't know that.

863
00:57:28.625 --> 00:57:31.833
Look here. We are 13 years apart.
How do you think it happened?

864
00:57:32.916 --> 00:57:34.250
What do you want to study?

865
00:57:34.333 --> 00:57:36.208
Molecular biology and genetics.

866
00:57:36.291 --> 00:57:37.375
At Boğaziçi too.

867
00:57:37.458 --> 00:57:38.916
- He has big aspirations.
- Yes.

868
00:57:39.000 --> 00:57:42.250
It's great that he has a goal.
Let him do it.

869
00:57:42.333 --> 00:57:44.250
Yeah, but he doesn't know
where he'll stay.

870
00:57:44.333 --> 00:57:45.791
I can barely look after myself.

871
00:57:46.416 --> 00:57:47.666
That's not true.

872
00:57:47.750 --> 00:57:49.208
Look around, kid.

873
00:57:50.500 --> 00:57:52.666
I'm not planning to live here anyway.

874
00:57:52.750 --> 00:57:53.666
Oh?

875
00:57:54.375 --> 00:57:56.083
Have you considered architecture?

876
00:57:56.166 --> 00:57:58.875
No, I'm interested in
molecular biology and genetics.

877
00:57:58.958 --> 00:57:59.958
You're determined.

878
00:58:00.500 --> 00:58:01.375
That's great.

879
00:58:02.458 --> 00:58:04.250
Your kitchen is unexpectedly clean.

880
00:58:05.458 --> 00:58:06.333
Bravo.

881
00:58:10.708 --> 00:58:12.125
You guys look cute.

882
00:58:12.750 --> 00:58:13.750
We broke up.

883
00:58:15.333 --> 00:58:16.208
For good.

884
00:58:18.208 --> 00:58:19.333
You'll make up.

885
00:58:46.125 --> 00:58:48.250
I'm writing them all down.

886
00:58:48.333 --> 00:58:50.333
I hope you can remember them.

887
00:58:54.666 --> 00:58:56.208
- Good evening, Semih.
- Yeah?

888
00:58:56.291 --> 00:58:59.250
- The notice to vacate we talked about.
- Okay, thanks.

889
00:58:59.333 --> 00:59:02.083
- No rush. Read it when you can.
- Thanks, all right.

890
00:59:03.000 --> 00:59:06.458
Be sure to read my notes
tomorrow morning before the meeting.

891
00:59:10.916 --> 00:59:12.041
Is everything okay?

892
00:59:13.041 --> 00:59:13.875
Yes.

893
00:59:15.250 --> 00:59:16.083
Okay.

894
00:59:17.583 --> 00:59:19.166
- What? It's fine.
- Okay.

895
00:59:19.250 --> 00:59:20.083
Yes.

896
00:59:21.083 --> 00:59:24.041
SEVCEN REAL ESTATE SERVICES
APARTMENTS FOR RENT

897
00:59:25.916 --> 00:59:27.916
Do you think I'd delete everything?

898
00:59:29.666 --> 00:59:32.250
You need to have an account first.

899
00:59:32.750 --> 00:59:35.333
But everyone has an account.
You wouldn't bother with it.

900
00:59:35.416 --> 00:59:37.125
Okay, let's say I have an account.

901
00:59:38.125 --> 00:59:39.333
Would I delete everything?

902
00:59:39.416 --> 00:59:40.625
You would.

903
00:59:41.541 --> 00:59:44.166
You would want her
to check your profile and be hurt.

904
00:59:49.416 --> 00:59:50.625
So she did it for me.

905
00:59:52.458 --> 00:59:55.583
Of course.
First and foremost, she did it for you.

906
00:59:57.083 --> 00:59:59.083
Then maybe for herself.

907
00:59:59.666 --> 01:00:01.000
So that she wouldn't hurt.

908
01:00:28.166 --> 01:00:29.875
Does this count as a bikini pic?

909
01:00:32.208 --> 01:00:33.791
You finally have an account?

910
01:00:34.333 --> 01:00:35.333
Follow me.

911
01:00:36.208 --> 01:00:38.041
Is it okay if I don't come with you?

912
01:00:38.958 --> 01:00:41.125
Can I drop you off at the campus?

913
01:00:41.750 --> 01:00:44.666
Are you bailing on me
because Defne is back in action?

914
01:00:44.750 --> 01:00:46.750
Not at all. I just have a ton of work.

915
01:00:48.375 --> 01:00:51.375
Now that you are moving out...

916
01:00:52.375 --> 01:00:55.458
What happens if Defne comes back?

917
01:00:56.083 --> 01:00:57.583
She will be royally screwed.

918
01:00:58.125 --> 01:00:59.791
She will find an empty apartment.

919
01:00:59.875 --> 01:01:01.875
She can't just delete photos and be done.

920
01:01:03.416 --> 01:01:05.375
Are you depressed or something?

921
01:01:05.458 --> 01:01:07.458
What's up with all these questions?

922
01:01:08.791 --> 01:01:10.041
I was just curious.

923
01:01:14.375 --> 01:01:15.208
I mean...

924
01:01:18.375 --> 01:01:20.208
Stuff like that. More or less.

925
01:01:22.208 --> 01:01:23.458
That's all.

926
01:01:27.541 --> 01:01:31.375
At least get up in your next presentation
so that it looks like you care.

927
01:01:33.916 --> 01:01:36.750
"I mean, stuff like that."

928
01:01:39.083 --> 01:01:41.500
I don't think you know
what you're talking about.

929
01:01:42.375 --> 01:01:45.958
I've been encouraging you all along.
"Come on, boy. Go on."

930
01:01:47.500 --> 01:01:48.583
But you're not there.

931
01:01:50.291 --> 01:01:52.500
We agree to everything you want.

932
01:01:53.250 --> 01:01:54.125
Don't we?

933
01:01:56.625 --> 01:01:58.750
I think I'm at fault here.

934
01:01:58.833 --> 01:02:00.791
Or you don't take your jobs seriously.

935
01:02:00.875 --> 01:02:03.500
And you have no clue
what it means to work as a team.

936
01:02:06.166 --> 01:02:07.125
Anyway, go.

937
01:02:07.208 --> 01:02:09.000
We'll talk once we calm down.

938
01:02:14.750 --> 01:02:16.000
Semih.

939
01:02:16.083 --> 01:02:17.958
This is shit. She is right.

940
01:02:18.833 --> 01:02:21.791
Have you no shame?
Is this what I told you yesterday?

941
01:02:21.875 --> 01:02:25.083
I'm kidding. She is being dramatic.
But I'll fix it, don't worry.

942
01:02:25.166 --> 01:02:27.625
- I wonder how you'll fix it.
- Stop being dramatic!

943
01:02:37.916 --> 01:02:38.750
Fuck.

944
01:03:10.666 --> 01:03:12.208
<i>What's up, Seksek?</i>

945
01:03:13.208 --> 01:03:14.333
<i>Good, you?</i>

946
01:03:14.416 --> 01:03:16.791
<i>Good. What happened? Did Defne come back?</i>

947
01:03:16.875 --> 01:03:18.875
<i>What are you talking about? Are you nuts?</i>

948
01:03:18.958 --> 01:03:20.958
<i>Then why don't you call me, you asshole?</i>

949
01:03:21.041 --> 01:03:22.875
<i>I thought it was
because you got back together.</i>

950
01:03:22.958 --> 01:03:25.416
<i>- Told you, I have a deadline.
- Good. Did you move out?</i>

951
01:03:25.500 --> 01:03:28.916
Sevcen Real Estate Services,
let's go clubbing!

952
01:03:29.000 --> 01:03:31.708
Sevcen Real Estate Services,
let's go clubbing!

953
01:03:50.333 --> 01:03:51.500
Semih?

954
01:03:51.583 --> 01:03:55.000
- How are you?
- Thanks, son. What happened?

955
01:03:55.083 --> 01:03:58.333
- I'm here to figure this thing out.
- No need to rush.

956
01:03:58.416 --> 01:04:02.708
Please, you called my mom.
I'll find a place in two weeks.

957
01:04:02.791 --> 01:04:06.041
- Okay, son.
- Okay. Say hi to Ms. Melahat.

958
01:04:06.125 --> 01:04:08.166
- Goodbye. Thanks.
<i>- Ciao.</i>

959
01:04:45.166 --> 01:04:46.416
Your touch feels lovely.

960
01:05:07.625 --> 01:05:10.375
The rent is great. You can move right in.

961
01:05:10.458 --> 01:05:12.208
It's really good. Okay.

962
01:05:12.291 --> 01:05:14.041
The landlord is a respectable man.

963
01:05:14.125 --> 01:05:17.916
He used to work in finance or something.
He probably never saw this place.

964
01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:20.583
He's waiting for a good tenant, but...

965
01:05:20.666 --> 01:05:23.125
Should I keep talking? What's happening?

966
01:05:23.208 --> 01:05:25.375
Where did you get your tattoo?
It's pretty.

967
01:05:25.458 --> 01:05:29.125
- I have a talented tattooist in Kadıköy.
- Cool.

968
01:05:29.208 --> 01:05:30.916
- But he's a little annoying.
- Yeah?

969
01:05:31.750 --> 01:05:33.083
Your tattoo is nice too.

970
01:05:33.166 --> 01:05:34.750
I designed most of them myself.

971
01:05:36.750 --> 01:05:38.333
It's a little aggressive, but...

972
01:06:18.625 --> 01:06:20.166
- Okay.
- Okay.

973
01:06:23.333 --> 01:06:24.166
Okay.

974
01:06:30.416 --> 01:06:32.500
Should we go to dinner or something?

975
01:06:34.958 --> 01:06:37.083
You won't end up saying I was too hot,

976
01:06:37.166 --> 01:06:40.458
so you couldn't resist
and stop yourself, right?

977
01:06:40.541 --> 01:06:42.791
No, I just meant a normal dinner.

978
01:06:43.625 --> 01:06:44.916
I don't know.

979
01:06:45.000 --> 01:06:48.916
Because then I might ask you,
"What happened? Did we lose our fire?"

980
01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:50.791
- Then you'll be screwed, okay?
- Look.

981
01:06:51.541 --> 01:06:53.000
I'll rent this place, okay?

982
01:06:53.083 --> 01:06:54.416
I'm okay, everything is fine.

983
01:06:55.291 --> 01:06:56.291
You heard me.

984
01:06:56.375 --> 01:06:58.833
The deposit's two months' rent.
No bargaining.

985
01:06:58.916 --> 01:07:02.833
The landlord's wife is lovely,
but you never know.

986
01:07:02.916 --> 01:07:04.500
It helps to meet them first...

987
01:07:04.583 --> 01:07:06.458
- Let's meet them!
- Okay.

988
01:07:07.083 --> 01:07:09.875
By the way, don't bargain with me.
I'll get one month's rent.

989
01:07:09.958 --> 01:07:11.500
I won't go down even if he does.

990
01:07:11.583 --> 01:07:14.416
Don't get it twisted
just because we almost had sex, okay?

991
01:07:14.500 --> 01:07:16.000
I never suggested that.

992
01:07:16.083 --> 01:07:19.041
If I gave it to all my customers,
I'd get kicked out of the neighborhood.

993
01:07:19.125 --> 01:07:21.041
Don't say that, Hande!
Will you open the door?

994
01:07:21.125 --> 01:07:24.333
I'm dying to know
who is chasing after you.

995
01:07:24.416 --> 01:07:25.541
What?

996
01:07:25.625 --> 01:07:29.041
You're running away so fast,
it makes me wonder who is chasing you.

997
01:07:29.125 --> 01:07:30.375
Nobody.

998
01:07:39.166 --> 01:07:40.916
- Welcome.
- Thanks.

999
01:07:46.625 --> 01:07:48.916
My uncle is waiting for me
to say something.

1000
01:07:50.458 --> 01:07:52.333
Are we done with the Hannover plan?

1001
01:07:53.541 --> 01:07:55.791
You said you didn't want to be
a government employee.

1002
01:07:55.875 --> 01:07:57.833
That's true. I don't.

1003
01:07:58.833 --> 01:08:00.125
We've been over this before.

1004
01:08:00.791 --> 01:08:03.375
My answer is the same.
I'll be suffocated there.

1005
01:08:03.458 --> 01:08:05.875
I don't speak the language.
What will I do there?

1006
01:08:06.375 --> 01:08:08.083
You can go, of course.

1007
01:08:08.833 --> 01:08:09.708
Thanks.

1008
01:08:10.833 --> 01:08:11.750
I know that.

1009
01:08:12.250 --> 01:08:15.000
But enough with the corporate life, right?

1010
01:08:15.958 --> 01:08:17.416
It's my job, Semih.

1011
01:08:17.500 --> 01:08:19.166
That's not what I meant.

1012
01:08:19.250 --> 01:08:21.208
Let's not make it our life.

1013
01:08:21.291 --> 01:08:23.166
Which is what you said, not me.

1014
01:08:23.250 --> 01:08:25.000
You're not coming, so I'm not going. Okay?

1015
01:08:25.583 --> 01:08:28.500
Don't you put the blame on me!
That's not the case.

1016
01:08:28.583 --> 01:08:30.916
I told you to go if you want to.

1017
01:08:32.166 --> 01:08:33.291
But I can't come.

1018
01:08:33.375 --> 01:08:35.250
I'm telling you, don't blame me.

1019
01:08:35.333 --> 01:08:39.583
I didn't even think about it
until you said I could earn euros.

1020
01:08:41.125 --> 01:08:43.291
It's not like I'm a money-grubber.

1021
01:08:43.375 --> 01:08:44.958
Your family is rich, of course.

1022
01:08:46.416 --> 01:08:47.375
Hey, uncle.

1023
01:08:48.416 --> 01:08:49.500
Are you in a meeting?

1024
01:08:51.250 --> 01:08:54.208
Okay, I'll say it quickly.

1025
01:08:54.291 --> 01:08:56.125
Semih and I thought about it.

1026
01:08:56.875 --> 01:08:58.375
His career is going well here.

1027
01:08:59.041 --> 01:09:00.708
So we think he should keep going.

1028
01:09:02.125 --> 01:09:03.583
Maybe in a few years...

1029
01:09:04.375 --> 01:09:05.750
Yes, but not now.

1030
01:09:05.833 --> 01:09:09.250
And they are considering me
for the assistant manager role.

1031
01:09:10.416 --> 01:09:13.833
If that happens, we will be good.

1032
01:09:15.958 --> 01:09:17.125
No, we are good.

1033
01:09:18.333 --> 01:09:21.333
We are good, but we will be better.

1034
01:09:22.166 --> 01:09:23.083
He says hi too.

1035
01:09:24.333 --> 01:09:25.208
Goodbye.

1036
01:09:27.750 --> 01:09:29.000
Is my nose that big?

1037
01:09:55.916 --> 01:09:58.750
It's great to be done
with the Hannover plan, right?

1038
01:10:00.416 --> 01:10:01.750
We live in Istanbul, Def.

1039
01:10:02.833 --> 01:10:04.458
Look at it. There is only one.

1040
01:10:05.958 --> 01:10:07.375
And there is only one of me.

1041
01:10:26.958 --> 01:10:28.291
I love you so much.

1042
01:10:30.291 --> 01:10:31.500
That felt so good.

1043
01:10:32.708 --> 01:10:33.791
Say it again.

1044
01:10:35.708 --> 01:10:36.666
I love you so much.

1045
01:10:42.916 --> 01:10:44.750
What's your happiness like?

1046
01:10:48.375 --> 01:10:49.750
It's partly cloudy.

1047
01:10:52.625 --> 01:10:54.625
But the sun will come out, right?

1048
01:10:59.791 --> 01:11:00.958
We'll make it come out.

1049
01:11:50.666 --> 01:11:52.000
What are you doing?

1050
01:11:52.833 --> 01:11:54.666
- We're waiting for you.
- I'm coming.

1051
01:11:54.750 --> 01:11:56.458
- Come on!
- Okay, just fuck off!

1052
01:12:26.791 --> 01:12:27.916
What are you doing?

1053
01:12:28.541 --> 01:12:29.375
Are you okay?

1054
01:12:29.458 --> 01:12:30.666
Yes, just taking a pic.

1055
01:12:33.291 --> 01:12:34.125
What's this?

1056
01:12:34.625 --> 01:12:35.875
Your deposit, Mr. Semih.

1057
01:12:37.125 --> 01:12:38.458
What deposit?

1058
01:12:38.541 --> 01:12:40.750
Or your realtor fee or something.

1059
01:12:41.375 --> 01:12:43.458
You've cried and talked about it all day.

1060
01:12:43.958 --> 01:12:46.208
- Give it back if you don't need it.
- No, okay.

1061
01:12:48.625 --> 01:12:49.833
You're so sweet.

1062
01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:54.000
Dude, you are a great guy,
but you aren't smart.

1063
01:12:55.916 --> 01:12:59.083
If I were you,
I wouldn't spend another minute here.

1064
01:13:00.500 --> 01:13:03.791
You're talented. You're a good artist.

1065
01:13:03.875 --> 01:13:05.166
So what are you doing?

1066
01:13:05.250 --> 01:13:06.625
Just get the fuck out.

1067
01:13:07.250 --> 01:13:08.500
And go where?

1068
01:13:09.000 --> 01:13:12.333
Get all the shit you draw,
get your portfolio and leave.

1069
01:13:12.416 --> 01:13:14.541
You can go to India or Japan.

1070
01:13:15.125 --> 01:13:16.625
You can make money everywhere.

1071
01:13:25.000 --> 01:13:26.666
I'll miss you guys.

1072
01:13:27.541 --> 01:13:28.416
Why?

1073
01:13:29.166 --> 01:13:30.625
I hear you're moving to Germany.

1074
01:13:30.708 --> 01:13:31.791
Germany?

1075
01:13:32.958 --> 01:13:34.208
As in Hannover, Germany?

1076
01:13:34.291 --> 01:13:37.875
Yeah. I'd also get away from here
if I could find a way.

1077
01:13:39.666 --> 01:13:42.875
Yeah, we were talking about it,
but we broke up.

1078
01:13:42.958 --> 01:13:44.083
Fuck. I didn't know.

1079
01:13:44.166 --> 01:13:46.916
It's okay, you couldn't know.
Don't be silly.

1080
01:13:47.000 --> 01:13:49.916
- Defne is leaving, huh?
- That's what she said.

1081
01:13:50.625 --> 01:13:53.625
Okay. She wanted to go, anyway.

1082
01:13:54.333 --> 01:13:56.666
- See you then.
- See you. Okay.

1083
01:14:47.708 --> 01:14:50.333
Come on. Get up.

1084
01:14:50.416 --> 01:14:52.291
- You have a fever, we should go.
- No.

1085
01:14:53.083 --> 01:14:54.625
I looked it up online.

1086
01:14:55.375 --> 01:14:57.375
Swine flu doesn't affect swines like me.

1087
01:14:58.375 --> 01:15:01.958
Your fever is 103 degrees.
Let's go to the hospital for an IV.

1088
01:15:02.041 --> 01:15:05.083
No. Don't you have work to do?

1089
01:15:05.166 --> 01:15:08.041
- How can I work when you're sick?
- Go away, Defne.

1090
01:15:08.833 --> 01:15:11.458
- I'll call the office. This is nonsense...
- Defne!

1091
01:15:11.541 --> 01:15:12.375
What?

1092
01:15:12.875 --> 01:15:15.375
You're talking nonsense. Come on, get up.

1093
01:15:18.875 --> 01:15:20.625
- What are you doing?
- Don't call anyone.

1094
01:15:20.708 --> 01:15:22.875
- What are you doing?
- Going to the bathroom.

1095
01:15:32.916 --> 01:15:33.875
Hello?

1096
01:15:33.958 --> 01:15:35.625
Do you have an available taxi?

1097
01:15:37.000 --> 01:15:40.791
Okay. Please send it
to Açelya Street, number 27.

1098
01:15:47.875 --> 01:15:49.041
Yes, we're canceling.

1099
01:15:49.125 --> 01:15:52.458
I called out to the driver
from our balcony.

1100
01:15:52.541 --> 01:15:54.541
But he didn't hear me.

1101
01:15:55.291 --> 01:15:56.208
I'm sorry.

1102
01:15:57.708 --> 01:15:58.541
Thank you.

1103
01:16:03.083 --> 01:16:03.916
Semih?

1104
01:16:05.666 --> 01:16:07.000
Semih, open the door.

1105
01:16:08.000 --> 01:16:09.666
You're acting like a kid, Semih!

1106
01:16:38.750 --> 01:16:39.583
Poyraz?

1107
01:16:40.416 --> 01:16:43.500
- I didn't mean to interrupt you.
- But you have. Go on.

1108
01:16:43.583 --> 01:16:45.916
A really cool Swedish DJ
has a concert tonight.

1109
01:16:46.958 --> 01:16:47.875
We're going there.

1110
01:16:48.500 --> 01:16:49.416
Okay, great.

1111
01:16:50.250 --> 01:16:52.833
Do you want to come?
I thought maybe we'd go together.

1112
01:16:54.541 --> 01:16:55.458
I can't, dude.

1113
01:16:55.541 --> 01:16:57.916
I have to finish these up
by tomorrow somehow.

1114
01:16:59.791 --> 01:17:00.791
Shall I call Nazım?

1115
01:17:00.875 --> 01:17:02.875
He got the tickets. I'll go with him.

1116
01:17:02.958 --> 01:17:04.208
- Oh?
- Yeah.

1117
01:17:04.916 --> 01:17:06.166
All right then.

1118
01:17:06.875 --> 01:17:08.375
- Okay?
- Okay, have fun.

1119
01:17:08.458 --> 01:17:09.625
- See you.
- Bye-bye.

1120
01:17:17.125 --> 01:17:19.625
Poyraz, have you spoken to Defne recently?

1121
01:17:19.708 --> 01:17:20.625
No.

1122
01:17:21.666 --> 01:17:23.041
Did something happen?

1123
01:17:23.125 --> 01:17:25.416
No. Nothing happened. I was just curious.

1124
01:17:25.500 --> 01:17:26.833
- Okay.
- Okay.

1125
01:17:26.916 --> 01:17:28.291
- Good luck.
- Thanks.

1126
01:17:44.458 --> 01:17:48.583
<i>Seksek, Defne is here,
and the atmosphere is great.</i>

1127
01:17:48.666 --> 01:17:50.041
<i>Just letting you know.</i>

1128
01:18:29.875 --> 01:18:31.208
Hey, what's up?

1129
01:18:33.083 --> 01:18:35.708
What did I tell you?
I told you I could make him come here!

1130
01:18:35.791 --> 01:18:37.583
Hey, where is Defne?

1131
01:18:38.166 --> 01:18:41.916
He is asking about Defne. She's not here.
We're here, having fun.

1132
01:18:42.000 --> 01:18:43.083
Look at his confused face.

1133
01:18:43.166 --> 01:18:45.041
You can't get over her. I told you.

1134
01:18:45.666 --> 01:18:47.083
Come on, we are having fun.

1135
01:18:47.166 --> 01:18:49.458
- Fuck off!
- Easy. Calm down.

1136
01:18:49.541 --> 01:18:51.541
- Are you nuts?
- Seksek.

1137
01:18:51.625 --> 01:18:54.833
- What are you doing?
- Okay, calm down. Stop being difficult.

1138
01:18:54.916 --> 01:18:56.958
- Shut up, Nazım.
- Get it together.

1139
01:18:58.041 --> 01:18:59.250
It's okay. Come on.

1140
01:18:59.333 --> 01:19:02.500
- What's going on?
- It's okay. Let's get drinks.

1141
01:19:10.375 --> 01:19:12.375
Are you upset because I invited Özge?

1142
01:19:12.458 --> 01:19:15.708
It's not about you.
I don't get what you're talking about.

1143
01:19:15.791 --> 01:19:18.708
I was third-wheeling that day,
so I thought I'd invite her.

1144
01:19:18.791 --> 01:19:21.583
It's not about you.
I didn't want it myself.

1145
01:19:21.666 --> 01:19:22.750
But thanks anyway.

1146
01:19:22.833 --> 01:19:24.416
By the way, I got this.

1147
01:19:28.375 --> 01:19:30.458
- What's this?
- Nazım gave it to me.

1148
01:19:37.083 --> 01:19:39.208
- What are you doing?
- What's this crap?

1149
01:19:39.291 --> 01:19:41.000
What the hell, guys?

1150
01:19:41.083 --> 01:19:45.041
- I'm gonna fuck your shit up!
- Let me go!

1151
01:19:51.708 --> 01:19:56.083
- Calm down!
- Fuck off!

1152
01:20:10.875 --> 01:20:12.541
Fuck you, Nazım!

1153
01:21:13.166 --> 01:21:14.041
Defne.

1154
01:21:17.625 --> 01:21:18.458
Hello?

1155
01:21:32.208 --> 01:21:33.166
Hey, man.

1156
01:21:34.000 --> 01:21:35.416
I'm Semih. Nice to meet you.

1157
01:21:38.000 --> 01:21:39.333
Look at Defne.

1158
01:21:40.500 --> 01:21:41.750
She's moving to Hannover.

1159
01:21:46.458 --> 01:21:47.666
I won't try anymore.

1160
01:21:50.416 --> 01:21:51.541
I won't waste my time.

1161
01:21:57.000 --> 01:21:58.541
Do you know Defne?

1162
01:22:04.000 --> 01:22:04.833
I'm gonna puke!

1163
01:22:13.166 --> 01:22:14.166
I couldn't.

1164
01:22:35.083 --> 01:22:37.875
I think I need to be with you.

1165
01:22:38.458 --> 01:22:40.250
I don't think. I'm sure.

1166
01:22:41.250 --> 01:22:44.541
And I was wondering where you have been.

1167
01:22:44.625 --> 01:22:46.000
I'm back now.

1168
01:22:47.375 --> 01:22:48.541
Do you have coffee?

1169
01:22:49.458 --> 01:22:50.666
We are closed.

1170
01:22:51.583 --> 01:22:53.958
I wasn't going to drink coffee, Ber.

1171
01:22:55.333 --> 01:22:56.208
Ber?

1172
01:22:58.500 --> 01:23:00.708
Could you show me some love right now?

1173
01:23:01.500 --> 01:23:04.791
Could you show yourself some love, Semih?

1174
01:23:05.666 --> 01:23:07.208
Yes, I know how to do that.

1175
01:23:08.500 --> 01:23:09.583
That's easy.

1176
01:23:12.791 --> 01:23:13.708
Sweetie.

1177
01:23:17.333 --> 01:23:18.541
You're too late.

1178
01:23:19.750 --> 01:23:23.291
I really enjoyed flirting too.

1179
01:23:24.750 --> 01:23:25.583
But I'm

1180
01:23:26.833 --> 01:23:28.583
over it now.

1181
01:23:30.458 --> 01:23:31.541
Why?

1182
01:23:33.583 --> 01:23:34.708
I'm pregnant.

1183
01:23:38.291 --> 01:23:40.625
- I'm pregnant!
- That's awesome.

1184
01:23:41.541 --> 01:23:43.041
Can I hug you now?

1185
01:24:10.916 --> 01:24:11.750
Semih.

1186
01:24:13.083 --> 01:24:15.541
Hey, get up. We'll be late, come on.

1187
01:24:20.291 --> 01:24:21.208
Good morning.

1188
01:24:22.666 --> 01:24:25.708
Good morning.
Get up or Ceyda will kill us.

1189
01:24:29.125 --> 01:24:29.958
What?

1190
01:24:31.541 --> 01:24:33.125
Don't be judgmental now.

1191
01:24:36.500 --> 01:24:38.208
What are you laughing at, jackass?

1192
01:24:40.000 --> 01:24:43.041
I'm just confused. That's all.

1193
01:24:43.125 --> 01:24:46.000
And I like this version of me, okay?

1194
01:24:46.083 --> 01:24:49.166
Why are you looking down on me?
Don't make me smack you.

1195
01:24:49.250 --> 01:24:50.583
I didn't say anything.

1196
01:24:51.458 --> 01:24:52.583
Shut up.

1197
01:24:53.583 --> 01:24:56.375
Let me do what I want for once.
You guys do all sorts of shit.

1198
01:24:56.458 --> 01:24:57.541
But when women do it,

1199
01:24:58.791 --> 01:24:59.750
you talk.

1200
01:25:02.833 --> 01:25:04.000
This is for Semih.

1201
01:25:04.666 --> 01:25:05.666
They gave it to me.

1202
01:25:06.250 --> 01:25:08.416
Def!

1203
01:25:08.916 --> 01:25:09.750
Defne!

1204
01:25:11.041 --> 01:25:11.875
Defne!

1205
01:25:13.750 --> 01:25:14.583
Defne!

1206
01:25:16.583 --> 01:25:17.458
Def!

1207
01:25:18.833 --> 01:25:22.416
Defne! Are you moving to Germany? Huh?

1208
01:25:23.000 --> 01:25:24.833
I am. Next week.

1209
01:25:24.916 --> 01:25:25.750
Why?

1210
01:25:26.291 --> 01:25:29.166
You can't ask me that anymore, Semih.

1211
01:25:30.333 --> 01:25:31.458
Is there someone else?

1212
01:25:33.000 --> 01:25:34.916
What difference does it make?

1213
01:25:36.458 --> 01:25:38.208
Why did you post those bikini pics?

1214
01:25:39.041 --> 01:25:41.375
- You think I gotta answer to you?
- No!

1215
01:25:41.958 --> 01:25:43.375
But I'm asking.

1216
01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:46.041
You said it was better to be offline.

1217
01:25:46.125 --> 01:25:49.166
- Defne, can we talk for a second?
- Talk about what?

1218
01:25:50.208 --> 01:25:51.375
- How are you?
- Good.

1219
01:25:53.208 --> 01:25:54.208
Really good?

1220
01:25:54.875 --> 01:25:57.958
- What do you want to know?
- I don't know what I want to know!

1221
01:25:58.958 --> 01:26:00.041
Are you over me?

1222
01:26:01.833 --> 01:26:02.916
We discussed it yesterday.

1223
01:26:05.125 --> 01:26:05.958
Yesterday?

1224
01:26:06.791 --> 01:26:07.625
Defne?

1225
01:26:10.333 --> 01:26:11.708
You don't remember, do you?

1226
01:26:12.958 --> 01:26:15.791
- You tried to puke, but you couldn't.
- I was...

1227
01:26:16.333 --> 01:26:17.583
I was talking to a dog.

1228
01:26:17.666 --> 01:26:19.083
You're asking if I'm over you?

1229
01:26:19.166 --> 01:26:21.500
I came to your place,
and Özge answered your door.

1230
01:26:21.583 --> 01:26:23.791
- No, she is with Nazım!
- Okay, whatever!

1231
01:26:24.541 --> 01:26:26.791
I just came here
to drop your phone off, okay?

1232
01:26:27.708 --> 01:26:30.500
- Goodbye.
- Def, I have a question!

1233
01:26:30.583 --> 01:26:32.875
At least tell me
if I said something wrong.

1234
01:26:34.208 --> 01:26:35.125
You didn't.

1235
01:26:36.416 --> 01:26:38.083
But you didn't say anything right either.

1236
01:26:40.041 --> 01:26:41.083
What did I say?

1237
01:26:41.166 --> 01:26:42.166
"What did I say?"

1238
01:26:44.666 --> 01:26:48.625
"What did I say? What did I do?
Was I in the right or wrong?"

1239
01:26:49.208 --> 01:26:51.041
It's always about you, Semih.

1240
01:26:52.250 --> 01:26:55.375
Where is Defne?
She is nowhere to be found!

1241
01:26:56.458 --> 01:26:59.166
She is nowhere to be found.

1242
01:27:01.250 --> 01:27:03.125
I kept waiting for a sign from you.

1243
01:27:04.083 --> 01:27:05.666
Something, anything...

1244
01:27:06.791 --> 01:27:10.000
Why do you think we broke up?
Have you ever thought about it?

1245
01:27:10.083 --> 01:27:11.250
You never asked.

1246
01:27:11.333 --> 01:27:13.166
You never asked, "Where are you going?"

1247
01:27:13.958 --> 01:27:15.083
You never even called.

1248
01:27:15.666 --> 01:27:16.500
You called.

1249
01:27:17.666 --> 01:27:19.583
Yes, but you don't remember it.

1250
01:27:23.166 --> 01:27:24.583
I can't believe your pride.

1251
01:27:27.333 --> 01:27:30.583
You're so busy with yourself
that you don't even think about me.

1252
01:27:33.708 --> 01:27:34.625
Never mind, Semih.

1253
01:27:36.125 --> 01:27:36.958
Never mind.

1254
01:27:38.458 --> 01:27:39.833
You have your own way.

1255
01:27:40.375 --> 01:27:41.333
Keep going.

1256
01:28:03.083 --> 01:28:03.958
Seksek!

1257
01:28:30.416 --> 01:28:31.416
Come visit me again.

1258
01:28:31.500 --> 01:28:33.583
- You sure?
- Of course, you idiot.

1259
01:28:34.208 --> 01:28:35.333
I'm your brother.

1260
01:28:38.333 --> 01:28:40.333
I can feel it. You'll get into Boğaziçi.

1261
01:28:42.375 --> 01:28:43.791
- I'm off.
- All right.

1262
01:28:46.000 --> 01:28:48.166
- Let me know when you land.
- Okay.

1263
01:28:48.250 --> 01:28:49.125
Take this.

1264
01:28:50.458 --> 01:28:53.375
- What is it?
- A mug. Give it to Mom.

1265
01:28:53.458 --> 01:28:54.333
All right.

1266
01:28:55.000 --> 01:28:56.541
- See you.
- Goodbye.

1267
01:29:05.041 --> 01:29:06.625
<i>Yezo, I'm really sick.</i>

1268
01:29:08.333 --> 01:29:10.333
<i>I know, it's due tomorrow.</i>

1269
01:29:11.416 --> 01:29:14.875
<i>Tell them my hard disk is broken
or I had a panic attack or something.</i>

1270
01:29:16.541 --> 01:29:19.000
<i>I couldn't finish it.
What will they do? Kill me?</i>

1271
01:29:19.083 --> 01:29:20.500
<i>I couldn't do it, okay?</i>

1272
01:29:49.041 --> 01:29:49.958
You haven't moved.

1273
01:29:50.750 --> 01:29:51.708
Ms. Ceyda?

1274
01:29:53.083 --> 01:29:54.125
Is it depression?

1275
01:29:55.291 --> 01:29:57.125
I don't know, maybe?

1276
01:29:58.125 --> 01:29:59.333
The breakup was hard on you.

1277
01:30:00.291 --> 01:30:03.541
It's not just that, Ms. Ceyda.
The breakup...

1278
01:30:03.625 --> 01:30:07.791
I really don't care
whatever the hell is going on with you.

1279
01:30:08.833 --> 01:30:10.416
You made a promise. Keep it.

1280
01:30:11.416 --> 01:30:12.500
It's not a game.

1281
01:30:12.583 --> 01:30:16.291
Sit down, cry, do the shit you need to do,
then finish what you started.

1282
01:30:17.458 --> 01:30:19.625
I don't understand.
Don't you feel embarrassed?

1283
01:30:19.708 --> 01:30:23.416
You looked me in the eye,
told me you'd do it and got an advance.

1284
01:30:23.500 --> 01:30:24.750
Have some dignity.

1285
01:30:25.958 --> 01:30:28.541
It's easy to be a champion
when you make your own rules.

1286
01:30:28.625 --> 01:30:29.958
That's not how life works.

1287
01:30:30.791 --> 01:30:33.875
I sometimes wonder if you are lazy
or just scared of competition.

1288
01:30:33.958 --> 01:30:35.791
Then I think, "Who cares?"

1289
01:30:35.875 --> 01:30:38.458
"Who cares what his problem is?
Why do I think about it?"

1290
01:30:38.541 --> 01:30:40.375
Honestly, who cares?

1291
01:30:40.458 --> 01:30:44.125
But life isn't just about
the path you are on.

1292
01:30:44.625 --> 01:30:45.583
Keep your word.

1293
01:30:45.666 --> 01:30:47.583
Don't stress me out
and ruin our relationship.

1294
01:30:49.416 --> 01:30:51.000
- I know, Ms. Ceyda...
- Fuck this.

1295
01:31:01.958 --> 01:31:02.791
<i>Hello?</i>

1296
01:31:02.875 --> 01:31:03.875
<i>Semih.</i>

1297
01:31:03.958 --> 01:31:05.000
<i>What's up, Mom?</i>

1298
01:31:06.791 --> 01:31:08.416
<i>Poyraz told me about some stuff.</i>

1299
01:31:09.500 --> 01:31:10.375
<i>Yeah.</i>

1300
01:31:11.166 --> 01:31:12.333
<i>How are you, my dear?</i>

1301
01:31:14.458 --> 01:31:15.291
<i>Good.</i>

1302
01:31:24.250 --> 01:31:25.250
<i>What happened?</i>

1303
01:31:25.833 --> 01:31:27.208
<i>Do you wanna tell me?</i>

1304
01:31:27.958 --> 01:31:28.791
<i>Nothing.</i>

1305
01:31:30.791 --> 01:31:33.708
<i>Son, Poyraz gave me your letter.</i>

1306
01:31:35.708 --> 01:31:37.083
<i>It isn't my letter.</i>

1307
01:31:37.708 --> 01:31:39.041
<i>It's your father's, dear.</i>

1308
01:31:39.875 --> 01:31:40.708
<i>I know.</i>

1309
01:31:41.750 --> 01:31:43.791
<i>But it was addressed to both of us.</i>

1310
01:31:45.833 --> 01:31:46.666
<i>Mom.</i>

1311
01:31:46.750 --> 01:31:47.583
<i>Yes?</i>

1312
01:31:50.375 --> 01:31:52.000
I went to the bathroom that day.

1313
01:31:54.416 --> 01:31:55.708
<i>When Dad left.</i>

1314
01:31:56.291 --> 01:31:57.291
<i>And it was there.</i>

1315
01:32:02.708 --> 01:32:04.083
He took everything.

1316
01:32:05.666 --> 01:32:07.250
He left nothing behind.

1317
01:32:09.125 --> 01:32:10.583
As if to say he won't return.

1318
01:32:12.166 --> 01:32:15.083
<i>But he kept his word. He never returned.</i>

1319
01:32:21.708 --> 01:32:24.708
That fucking thing was there
the morning Defne left me.

1320
01:32:25.583 --> 01:32:28.500
<i>My dear, why did you take it
in the first place?</i>

1321
01:32:29.458 --> 01:32:31.500
That was the only thing he left behind.

1322
01:32:34.458 --> 01:32:35.500
What is it?

1323
01:32:36.916 --> 01:32:40.291
<i>I think we were
in Düsseldorf or something.</i>

1324
01:32:40.375 --> 01:32:41.916
<i>We bought it there.</i>

1325
01:32:42.916 --> 01:32:44.541
<i>It's nothing special.</i>

1326
01:32:46.125 --> 01:32:48.375
<i>I don't think he left it on purpose.</i>

1327
01:32:49.708 --> 01:32:51.833
<i>He just forgot about it in his hurry.</i>

1328
01:32:53.000 --> 01:32:55.125
<i>Or else, he'd have taken his sins with him
if he could.</i>

1329
01:33:01.583 --> 01:33:02.541
I have them.

1330
01:33:03.333 --> 01:33:04.166
<i>What?</i>

1331
01:33:07.708 --> 01:33:08.541
His sins.

1332
01:33:09.666 --> 01:33:10.583
I have them.

1333
01:33:14.250 --> 01:33:16.375
I can never tell people<i>,</i> "Don't leave."

1334
01:33:31.291 --> 01:33:32.750
<i>How did you deal with it?</i>

1335
01:33:33.958 --> 01:33:34.958
<i>I just felt sad.</i>

1336
01:33:35.541 --> 01:33:36.666
<i>I know that.</i>

1337
01:33:37.208 --> 01:33:40.041
<i>What else could I do, Semih?
What else, my dear?</i>

1338
01:33:40.125 --> 01:33:41.750
<i>I just felt completely sad.</i>

1339
01:33:42.708 --> 01:33:44.750
<i>Don't be so afraid.</i>

1340
01:33:44.833 --> 01:33:47.458
<i>Your dad did teach me
what to do with a broken heart.</i>

1341
01:33:47.541 --> 01:33:48.625
<i>But I don't know.</i>

1342
01:33:50.000 --> 01:33:52.666
<i>You never told me.
What do you do with a broken heart?</i>

1343
01:33:54.583 --> 01:33:57.208
<i>Every heart breaks differently, son.</i>

1344
01:34:51.166 --> 01:34:52.166
<i>Well, I'm off.</i>

1345
01:34:53.541 --> 01:34:56.500
<i>I was just checking out
the last work you sent in.</i>

1346
01:34:56.583 --> 01:34:58.583
Yes, it's done.

1347
01:34:58.666 --> 01:35:00.708
Yes. Good job, congratulations.

1348
01:35:04.166 --> 01:35:05.583
I need to ask you something.

1349
01:35:08.583 --> 01:35:10.000
Why did you come?

1350
01:35:12.000 --> 01:35:13.875
I felt that you didn't hear me.

1351
01:35:13.958 --> 01:35:18.041
I mean,
I felt that I didn't really matter to you.

1352
01:35:18.125 --> 01:35:22.083
I also truly care about
your mom, my teacher, Ms. Elif.

1353
01:35:22.708 --> 01:35:23.541
That's why.

1354
01:35:24.250 --> 01:35:25.375
Thank you.

1355
01:35:26.583 --> 01:35:28.458
- Take care.
- You too.

1356
01:35:40.541 --> 01:35:43.750
All right. Here you go,
this is your guitar.

1357
01:35:43.833 --> 01:35:45.000
My guitar?

1358
01:35:45.083 --> 01:35:46.875
Begüm is waiting for your call.

1359
01:35:47.750 --> 01:35:48.583
Who is Begüm?

1360
01:35:48.666 --> 01:35:49.708
Your guitar teacher.

1361
01:35:50.708 --> 01:35:52.708
Semih, I can't believe it.

1362
01:36:05.458 --> 01:36:07.041
<i>Apologize to my grandma.</i>

1363
01:36:07.625 --> 01:36:08.708
<i>She loved you.</i>

1364
01:36:09.208 --> 01:36:10.750
<i>I don't know why.</i>

1365
01:36:22.875 --> 01:36:27.375
MÜNEVVER GÜNAY
REST IN PEACE

1366
01:36:51.083 --> 01:36:52.250
I like it.

1367
01:37:05.583 --> 01:37:07.916
HABITS GIVE ME
AN ITCH - CONSTANTLY

1368
01:37:08.625 --> 01:37:11.333
<i>I guess people get them on a whim.
It always happens.</i>

1369
01:37:12.041 --> 01:37:13.000
<i>But it's not that easy.</i>

1370
01:37:14.000 --> 01:37:17.041
<i>You have to think of the future.
Right, sir?</i>

1371
01:37:17.125 --> 01:37:20.916
I mean, you have to plan
your vacations accordingly.

1372
01:37:21.500 --> 01:37:26.458
You have to think, "I've adopted this dog,
but can I take care of it?"

1373
01:37:27.250 --> 01:37:28.750
Yes, people love their dogs.

1374
01:37:28.833 --> 01:37:32.416
But it's not enough to love them.
Love is not everything, sir.

1375
01:37:32.500 --> 01:37:36.208
For instance, you have to take them out,

1376
01:37:36.291 --> 01:37:38.625
let them run,
give them whatever they want.

1377
01:37:39.708 --> 01:37:43.333
But dogs have
an interesting characteristic too.

1378
01:37:43.416 --> 01:37:45.125
They love whoever their owner is.

1379
01:37:45.916 --> 01:37:47.083
They are full of love.

1380
01:37:48.166 --> 01:37:50.208
Everyone claims they'll take care of them.

1381
01:37:50.708 --> 01:37:52.125
But they barely last three days.

1382
01:37:52.208 --> 01:37:53.625
Then they dump them on the street.

1383
01:37:54.791 --> 01:37:58.083
If you won't be able to take care of it,
then why would you adopt it?

1384
01:37:58.166 --> 01:37:59.291
Am I right, sir?

1385
01:38:01.000 --> 01:38:03.958
But honestly,
I think you are trustworthy, sir.

1386
01:38:05.166 --> 01:38:06.750
You won't abandon your dog, right?

1387
01:38:08.291 --> 01:38:09.500
- Right?
- What?

1388
01:38:09.583 --> 01:38:11.208
- You won't abandon it.
- No.

1389
01:38:14.375 --> 01:38:16.916
I think I know this guy from somewhere.

1390
01:38:17.875 --> 01:38:20.333
What do you think?

1391
01:38:21.000 --> 01:38:22.000
Can he come with me?

1392
01:38:22.958 --> 01:38:23.958
I mean...

1393
01:38:26.250 --> 01:38:28.625
Rüstem. Can I call you Rüstem?

1394
01:38:29.750 --> 01:38:30.833
Okay, thanks.

1395
01:38:33.000 --> 01:38:34.750
We'll see how it goes, Rüstem.

1396
01:38:36.625 --> 01:38:38.375
Try to put up with me a little bit.

1397
01:38:40.791 --> 01:38:42.833
I've just started learning some things.

1398
01:38:44.416 --> 01:38:45.250
I'll admit.

1399
01:38:51.875 --> 01:38:53.333
But you can trust me.

1400
01:38:58.416 --> 01:38:59.250
Yes.

1401
01:39:02.333 --> 01:39:03.458
You can trust me.

1402
01:39:29.333 --> 01:39:30.208
Semih?

1403
01:39:33.916 --> 01:39:34.750
Wow!

1404
01:39:37.708 --> 01:39:38.541
Who is this?

1405
01:39:39.500 --> 01:39:40.333
Rüstem.

1406
01:39:42.500 --> 01:39:45.083
You little bad boy! You are so cute.

1407
01:39:52.041 --> 01:39:52.875
How are you?

1408
01:39:53.625 --> 01:39:56.416
I'm good. Things are okay.

1409
01:39:57.333 --> 01:39:58.333
- You?
- Good.

1410
01:39:59.250 --> 01:40:01.416
I got used to living in Germany.

1411
01:40:04.750 --> 01:40:06.125
I came here for vacation.

1412
01:40:06.625 --> 01:40:07.750
I'm going back today.

1413
01:40:08.750 --> 01:40:09.583
Cool.

1414
01:40:12.666 --> 01:40:13.833
I'm glad to see you.

1415
01:40:14.416 --> 01:40:15.500
Me too.

1416
01:40:16.416 --> 01:40:18.041
What a crazy coincidence.

1417
01:40:18.708 --> 01:40:19.708
What happened?

1418
01:40:19.791 --> 01:40:20.750
- To what?
- This.

1419
01:40:21.666 --> 01:40:24.041
"Habits give me an itch - constantly."

1420
01:40:25.916 --> 01:40:27.708
- It's from Turgut Uyar.
- It's nice.

1421
01:40:29.208 --> 01:40:30.041
It always is.

1422
01:40:31.583 --> 01:40:34.500
But I don't know
if I would say that about you.

1423
01:40:36.583 --> 01:40:38.625
Okay, what would you say about me?

1424
01:40:39.750 --> 01:40:40.583
I don't know.

1425
01:40:43.291 --> 01:40:44.541
You're a firework.

1426
01:40:45.750 --> 01:40:47.250
Exploding in the darkness.

1427
01:40:49.916 --> 01:40:52.125
As I remember it,
you said all you wanted to say.

1428
01:40:55.333 --> 01:40:56.750
It's nice to remember, right?

1429
01:40:59.458 --> 01:41:00.833
It's so nice to remember.

1430
01:41:02.791 --> 01:41:03.666
Come on.
